WEBVTT

﻿1

00:01:53.514 --> 00:01:54.714
Mona, I'm on upper county.


00:01:54.715 --> 00:01:57.217
Stutz's cows are
in the road again.


00:01:57.218 --> 00:01:58.684
Again?


00:01:58.686 --> 00:02:00.420
Yeah, I'm gonna set flares


00:02:00.421 --> 00:02:02.255
and go get 'em.


00:02:02.256 --> 00:02:03.590
Should I log that?


00:02:03.591 --> 00:02:06.126
No, I'll log it.


00:02:06.127 --> 00:02:08.695
Stutz house...


00:02:08.696 --> 00:02:11.264
Road.


00:02:11.265 --> 00:02:12.264
It's logged.


00:02:15.469 --> 00:02:17.536
Come on now, cow, get
out of the road.


00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.143
Hey, Mona.


00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:28.681
Uh, Mona, I got a shoe here.


00:02:28.682 --> 00:02:29.781
A shoe?


00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:35.487
Yeah, like, a girl's shoe.


00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.191
Oh.


00:02:38.192 --> 00:02:39.926
Should I bring it in?


00:02:39.927 --> 00:02:41.693
A shoe?


00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.763
Hang on a second.


00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.748
Hello?


00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.825
Is someone there?


00:03:12.826 --> 00:03:14.293
Oh.


00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:17.230
Mona.


00:03:17.231 --> 00:03:20.433
Uh, Mona? Mona.


00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:21.768
Mona!


00:03:21.769 --> 00:03:23.203
I can hear you.


00:03:23.204 --> 00:03:24.204
Uh...


00:03:24.205 --> 00:03:25.204
I got a...


00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:29.943
I got a... I got a woman
on the ground here.


00:03:29.944 --> 00:03:31.444
Has there been a wreck?


00:03:31.445 --> 00:03:34.479
No, no, no, she's, uh...


00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:39.686
Oh... Ugh.


00:03:39.687 --> 00:03:41.254
What?


00:03:41.255 --> 00:03:43.690
Uh, she's, uh...


00:03:43.691 --> 00:03:44.724
She's dead.


00:03:44.725 --> 00:03:45.792
Uh...


00:03:45.793 --> 00:03:47.894
Hey, Mona.


00:03:47.895 --> 00:03:49.429
What?


00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:51.397
Are you sure?


00:03:51.398 --> 00:03:53.666
Who's at the scene?


00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:55.235
T.J.


00:03:55.236 --> 00:03:57.237
Oh, no. Is he alone?


00:03:57.238 --> 00:03:58.838
Is he all right?


00:03:58.839 --> 00:03:59.872
No, no. I'll be right there.


00:03:59.873 --> 00:04:00.973
Okay.


00:04:13.654 --> 00:04:14.954
I got to say,


00:04:14.955 --> 00:04:16.589
didn't expect to be
dealing with a homicide


00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:17.624
my first week here.


00:04:17.625 --> 00:04:19.792
This happen often? No.


00:04:19.793 --> 00:04:22.495
First homicide here
since I was a teenager.


00:04:22.496 --> 00:04:24.330
Thought you were
from Cleveland.


00:04:24.331 --> 00:04:26.366
Cleveland pd. I grew up here.


00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:27.867
Is your family still here?


00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:29.502
Yeah, they're around.


00:04:29.503 --> 00:04:30.603
You see them?


00:04:30.604 --> 00:04:31.838
Oh, I see them all the time.


00:04:31.839 --> 00:04:33.705
They don't see me much.


00:04:38.279 --> 00:04:39.512
You all right, T.J...?


00:04:39.513 --> 00:04:40.913
Thanks, chief.


00:04:40.914 --> 00:04:42.415
Where's skid?


00:04:42.416 --> 00:04:44.384
Uh, went to get the
owner there, Mr. stutz.


00:04:44.385 --> 00:04:46.552
All right, let's set
some perimeters.


00:04:46.553 --> 00:04:48.655
And anything within 100 yards
that didn't grow here,


00:04:48.656 --> 00:04:50.556
I want it marked and bagged.


00:04:50.557 --> 00:04:51.924
- You mean by me?
- Yeah, T.J..


00:04:51.925 --> 00:04:54.294
I'll help you in a minute.


00:04:54.295 --> 00:04:56.696
- Doc?
- Oh, hey, chief.


00:04:56.697 --> 00:05:00.299
I think it's safe to say
we have a homicide here.


00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.337
She's amish.


00:05:04.338 --> 00:05:05.505
Are you sure about that?


00:05:05.506 --> 00:05:06.873
Well...


00:05:06.874 --> 00:05:10.310
No nail Polish,
visible piercings,


00:05:10.311 --> 00:05:11.511
no makeup, no hair dye,


00:05:11.512 --> 00:05:13.846
and that dress is amish.


00:05:13.847 --> 00:05:15.514
Hey, chief!


00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.522
Where is she? Is she English?


00:05:22.523 --> 00:05:24.324
We don't know yet.


00:05:24.325 --> 00:05:26.893
Did you see or hear anything out
of the ordinary last night?


00:05:26.894 --> 00:05:28.328
Uh, it would be better


00:05:28.329 --> 00:05:29.961
if you could ask
me the questions.


00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:34.801
Please, I cannot speak to her.


00:05:34.802 --> 00:05:37.537
Mr. stutz, you don't have to
speak to Kate burkholder,


00:05:37.538 --> 00:05:39.505
but you do have to speak
to the chief of police,


00:05:39.506 --> 00:05:40.540
and that happens to be me.


00:05:40.541 --> 00:05:41.641
You can do that here,


00:05:41.642 --> 00:05:42.775
or you can do it
at the station.


00:05:42.776 --> 00:05:44.544
It's your choice.


00:05:44.545 --> 00:05:46.045
I did not see anything.


00:05:46.046 --> 00:05:47.513
Any strange vehicles
on the road?


00:05:47.514 --> 00:05:48.781
Did you hear anything?


00:05:48.782 --> 00:05:51.684
I was asleep. I go
to bed at 9:00.


00:05:51.685 --> 00:05:53.419
- May I go?
- Yes.


00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.787
But we may need to
speak to you again.


00:05:54.788 --> 00:05:55.922
If you leave town,


00:05:55.923 --> 00:05:57.357
tell bishop troyers
how to reach you.


00:05:57.358 --> 00:05:58.791
I'm not going anywhere.


00:05:58.792 --> 00:06:02.862
Please, take her off my land.
Chief.


00:06:02.863 --> 00:06:04.797
We're gonna have a problem
plastering for marks


00:06:04.798 --> 00:06:06.366
until this snow melts.


00:06:06.367 --> 00:06:07.700
Hey! Chief!


00:06:07.701 --> 00:06:09.035
Yeah?


00:06:09.036 --> 00:06:10.402
I think you ought to see this.


00:06:12.606 --> 00:06:14.374
There it is.


00:06:14.375 --> 00:06:16.676
It's him.


00:06:16.677 --> 00:06:18.144
That's impossible.


00:06:18.145 --> 00:06:19.746
I don't know about impossible,


00:06:19.747 --> 00:06:22.381
but it's so damned unlikely.


00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:25.818
You okay?


00:06:25.819 --> 00:06:27.420
Yeah, fine.


00:06:27.421 --> 00:06:29.689
What is that?


00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:32.959
- We had a serial killer
around here years ago.


00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:35.428
He killed five young
women back in the '90s.


00:06:35.429 --> 00:06:36.796
And then he just stopped.


00:06:36.797 --> 00:06:39.532
- We thought maybe he
died or just left or...


00:06:39.533 --> 00:06:41.434
We called him slaughterhouse.


00:06:41.435 --> 00:06:43.469
And that was his signature:


00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.004
Roman numerals, just like that.


00:06:45.005 --> 00:06:46.873
All of them amish?


00:06:46.874 --> 00:06:48.574
This would be the first.


00:06:48.575 --> 00:06:50.709
- If it was him,
there would be a...


00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:55.681
Was that... Postmortem?


00:06:55.682 --> 00:06:57.617
No.


00:06:57.618 --> 00:07:00.753
- So see, she was
hung upside down,


00:07:00.754 --> 00:07:02.054
then bled to death.


00:07:02.055 --> 00:07:04.457
And see that?


00:07:04.458 --> 00:07:06.993
That's the blood track
residue right there.


00:07:06.994 --> 00:07:08.561
Skid, go to bishop troyers


00:07:08.562 --> 00:07:10.196
and ask him if he knows
of an amish girl 18 to 21


00:07:10.197 --> 00:07:11.197
who's gone missing.


00:07:11.198 --> 00:07:14.032
You got it, chief.


00:07:24.178 --> 00:07:26.078
- Chief burkholder, is it
true they found a body...


00:07:26.079 --> 00:07:27.212
not now, I'm afraid.


00:07:29.482 --> 00:07:30.616
Hey, who called?


00:07:30.617 --> 00:07:32.819
Everybody.


00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:34.754
The paper's called 11 times.


00:07:34.755 --> 00:07:37.089
- Uh, channel 8 news...
- Already?


00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:39.759
- Well, they monitor the
police radio, right?


00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:42.061
So T.J.. Mentions the
word "slaughterhouse"


00:07:42.062 --> 00:07:43.496
on the air when
calling in the apb.


00:07:43.497 --> 00:07:44.630
I know!


00:07:44.631 --> 00:07:45.998
That got some attention.


00:07:45.999 --> 00:07:48.034
- Uh, the mayor called.
- Wonderful.


00:07:48.035 --> 00:07:50.937
- Yeah, it gets better.
- He's on his way over.


00:07:50.938 --> 00:07:52.839
- Right.
- Well, you know how it is.


00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:55.200
Half the town's heard already.
Other half will know by noon.


00:07:56.477 --> 00:07:57.476
Thank you.


00:07:59.712 --> 00:08:01.948
- That farmer, chief, why
didn't he speak to you?


00:08:01.949 --> 00:08:03.483
I'm under the ban.


00:08:03.484 --> 00:08:04.784
In English?


00:08:04.785 --> 00:08:07.487
- I left the amish
community when I was 18.


00:08:07.488 --> 00:08:08.921
You were amish?


00:08:08.922 --> 00:08:10.490
I was.


00:08:10.491 --> 00:08:11.657
For real?


00:08:11.658 --> 00:08:12.658
For real.


00:08:12.659 --> 00:08:13.826
Huh.


00:08:13.827 --> 00:08:15.561
Thought that was sort
of a lifetime deal.


00:08:15.562 --> 00:08:17.263
Well, usually it is.


00:08:17.264 --> 00:08:18.564
Ah.


00:08:18.565 --> 00:08:19.765
They don't talk to you?


00:08:19.766 --> 00:08:21.267
- Well, they try not
to be rude about it,


00:08:21.268 --> 00:08:22.268
but those are the rules.


00:08:22.269 --> 00:08:23.703
When I'm working,


00:08:23.704 --> 00:08:25.004
eventually they'll
answer a question.


00:08:25.005 --> 00:08:26.806
Mayor alert.


00:08:26.807 --> 00:08:28.508
Your, um, family too?


00:08:28.509 --> 00:08:29.809
What about them?


00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:31.177
They don't speak to you?


00:08:31.178 --> 00:08:32.278
- Nichols, I need you to focus


00:08:32.279 --> 00:08:33.645
on what we're dealing with here.


00:08:35.248 --> 00:08:36.516
Auggie.


00:08:36.517 --> 00:08:37.683
Hey, uh, you got a minute?


00:08:37.684 --> 00:08:39.252
Yeah, come in.


00:08:39.253 --> 00:08:40.253
Mr. mayor.


00:08:40.254 --> 00:08:41.587
Sure I can't make you


00:08:41.588 --> 00:08:42.855
a nice herbal tea, Mr. mayor?


00:08:42.856 --> 00:08:45.992
Oh, I'll call you if we
need anything, Mona.


00:08:45.993 --> 00:08:47.727
- Hi. I won't keep you.
- Okay.


00:08:47.728 --> 00:08:49.762
Um...


00:08:49.763 --> 00:08:51.931
I just... what's
your read on this?


00:08:51.932 --> 00:08:53.566
Do we need to bring
in the state bureau?


00:08:53.567 --> 00:08:55.201
- Bci?
- Mm.


00:08:55.202 --> 00:08:56.269
Not at this point.


00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:58.037
Why? What's your concern?


00:08:58.038 --> 00:09:00.106
- Just concerned this is
going to be very demanding


00:09:00.107 --> 00:09:02.275
on a small department with a
brand-new chief of police.


00:09:02.276 --> 00:09:04.176
I've been here six months.


00:09:04.177 --> 00:09:06.145
- Kate, if this is the
slaughterhouse killer again,


00:09:06.146 --> 00:09:07.847
they'll send us a profiler.


00:09:07.848 --> 00:09:10.082
- I don't think that we can
assume it's slaughterhouse.


00:09:10.083 --> 00:09:12.084
I mean, this is an amish girl.
The other girls were...


00:09:12.085 --> 00:09:13.553
yeah, Kate...


00:09:13.554 --> 00:09:14.687
Kate, it's my call.


00:09:14.688 --> 00:09:17.123
And, actually, her being amish


00:09:17.124 --> 00:09:18.591
makes this particularly
sensitive.


00:09:18.592 --> 00:09:20.026
I think we could benefit from...


00:09:20.027 --> 00:09:21.961
auggie, I have led seven
homicide investigations.


00:09:21.962 --> 00:09:23.262
And you know what?


00:09:23.263 --> 00:09:25.965
All seven guys are now
sitting in youngstown.


00:09:25.966 --> 00:09:27.266
Do you not want a profiler?


00:09:27.267 --> 00:09:29.669
It won't come out
of your budget.


00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:31.736
You already called bci.


00:09:33.206 --> 00:09:34.574
- Yeah, yeah...
- Yeah.


00:09:34.575 --> 00:09:35.875
And they're sending
over a profiler.


00:09:35.876 --> 00:09:37.243
It's still your case.


00:09:37.244 --> 00:09:39.579
Oh, come on, don't look
at me like that, Kate.


00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:41.247
He's supposed to be very good.


00:09:41.248 --> 00:09:43.081
Course he is.


00:09:45.285 --> 00:09:48.621
Jay...


00:09:48.622 --> 00:09:51.123
Jay, you haven't
answered the question.


00:09:51.124 --> 00:09:52.625
What's your point?


00:09:52.626 --> 00:09:54.961
- Why me, and why now?


00:09:54.962 --> 00:09:56.228
- Why'd I give you
an assignment?


00:09:56.229 --> 00:09:57.663
You're still on active duty.


00:09:57.664 --> 00:09:58.931
That four-month
bender you've been on


00:09:58.932 --> 00:10:00.099
doesn't entitle you...


00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.834
- whoa, whoa, now.
- Hold on, now.


00:10:01.835 --> 00:10:04.770
I think a four-month bender
entitles me to, uh...


00:10:04.771 --> 00:10:06.639
- John, work the case,
or I'm suspending you.


00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:07.740
It's up to you.


00:10:07.741 --> 00:10:09.609
Any questions?


00:10:09.610 --> 00:10:11.777
Eh, just one.


00:10:11.778 --> 00:10:13.612
Why are you always such a jerk?


00:10:38.771 --> 00:10:41.007
Nichols?


00:10:41.008 --> 00:10:42.041
Right here, chief.


00:10:42.042 --> 00:10:43.809
Do a nationwide check:


00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:47.079
All deaths by exsanguination.


00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:48.881
- Plus anything with
Roman numerals.


00:10:48.882 --> 00:10:51.651
I figure we're looking for
murders six through ten.


00:10:51.652 --> 00:10:53.285
- Exactly.
- And, Mona?


00:10:53.286 --> 00:10:54.820
That's me.


00:10:54.821 --> 00:10:56.989
- Send T.J.. Down to the
county clerk's office.


00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:58.057
- Sure.
- What do you need?


00:10:58.058 --> 00:10:59.358
I want a list


00:10:59.359 --> 00:11:01.093
of all abandoned
properties in the county.


00:11:01.094 --> 00:11:02.395
Because?


00:11:02.396 --> 00:11:04.163
- Well, that girl wasn't
killed in the field.


00:11:04.164 --> 00:11:05.364
It had to be somewhere remote.


00:11:05.365 --> 00:11:07.700
And we'll search them
all as crime scenes.


00:11:07.701 --> 00:11:09.268
Okay, boss.


00:11:09.269 --> 00:11:10.703
Oh, do you want your messages?


00:11:10.704 --> 00:11:12.672
Anything important?


00:11:12.673 --> 00:11:14.674
Mayor wants a progress report.


00:11:14.675 --> 00:11:16.174
Course he does.


00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:20.045
- Hey, you know a
storm's coming in.


00:11:34.093 --> 00:11:37.262
Hi, Sarah.


00:11:42.735 --> 00:11:45.070
I need to see Jacob.


00:11:51.877 --> 00:11:53.913
Jacob?


00:11:53.914 --> 00:11:56.047
Your sister is here.


00:12:23.509 --> 00:12:26.211
That cabinet, did you make it?


00:12:29.048 --> 00:12:32.351
It's beautiful.


00:12:32.352 --> 00:12:35.788
Why you've come here?


00:12:35.789 --> 00:12:39.759
There's been a murder.


00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:42.495
You're here as a policeman?


00:12:42.496 --> 00:12:44.897
Yes.


00:12:44.898 --> 00:12:47.800
All right, then.


00:12:47.801 --> 00:12:49.834
An amish girl.


00:12:52.538 --> 00:12:54.073
You know this for sure?


00:12:54.074 --> 00:12:55.407
We'll know soon enough,


00:12:55.408 --> 00:12:59.245
but, um...


00:12:59.246 --> 00:13:02.982
Jacob, she was bled to death.


00:13:02.983 --> 00:13:06.017
I need to talk to you
about Daniel Lapp.


00:13:22.802 --> 00:13:24.035
What is it you want to know?


00:13:27.506 --> 00:13:30.009
- I need to know
that he's dead.


00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:31.844
- And you come to me for this?


00:13:31.845 --> 00:13:34.180
- If he is alive, he
is killing again.


00:13:34.181 --> 00:13:36.982
And if not, someone
is copying him.


00:13:36.983 --> 00:13:39.819
Jacob, I need to know
what happened that night.


00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:42.521
You know what happened.


00:13:42.522 --> 00:13:43.923
Dad took him in the buggy.


00:13:43.924 --> 00:13:46.292
And you went with him?


00:13:46.293 --> 00:13:49.128
Where?


00:13:49.129 --> 00:13:51.162
The old grain mill.


00:13:54.867 --> 00:13:55.868
Was he dead?


00:13:55.869 --> 00:13:59.839
Must have been.


00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:01.306
All that blood.


00:14:04.443 --> 00:14:06.612
Did Dad bury him?


00:14:06.613 --> 00:14:08.881
Couldn't see.


00:14:08.882 --> 00:14:10.916
I was outside. Dad
took him inside.


00:14:10.917 --> 00:14:13.085
- Wait.
- So you don't know if he's dead?


00:14:13.086 --> 00:14:16.856
- Kate, I swore to Dad I
would never speak of this,


00:14:16.857 --> 00:14:18.356
and you did too.


00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:25.898
- Come with me
to the old mill.


00:14:25.899 --> 00:14:26.899
Why?


00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:28.567
I need to be sure, Jacob.


00:14:28.568 --> 00:14:30.870
You mean dig him up?


00:14:30.871 --> 00:14:32.871
Are you listening to yourself?


00:14:35.574 --> 00:14:38.143
You want to know
about Daniel Lapp,


00:14:38.144 --> 00:14:40.312
go talk to Lucas Holtz.


00:14:40.313 --> 00:14:42.881
He managed the Lapp
farm for years.


00:14:44.583 --> 00:14:46.952
Give you a reason


00:14:46.953 --> 00:14:49.921
to apologize for leaving
without a word.


00:14:52.391 --> 00:14:54.659
The man you were gonna marry.


00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:03.002
- That's it?
- That's all you have to say?


00:15:03.003 --> 00:15:05.571
It was a dark and ugly thing.


00:15:05.572 --> 00:15:08.941
We all felt pain
from that time.


00:15:08.942 --> 00:15:10.642
I know that.


00:15:14.914 --> 00:15:16.982
You smiled at Daniel Lapp


00:15:16.983 --> 00:15:20.119
for months when he
worked for Mom and Dad.


00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:23.154
I saw you.


00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:27.393
I know what I did.


00:15:27.394 --> 00:15:30.129
And I know what he did to me.


00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:32.431
- How can you be sure
that Lapp is this man,


00:15:32.432 --> 00:15:34.667
this... this slaughterhouse?


00:15:34.668 --> 00:15:37.069
I'm not.


00:15:37.070 --> 00:15:40.605
But after he was gone,
the killing stopped.


00:15:43.242 --> 00:15:44.943
I've made my peace with this.


00:15:46.545 --> 00:15:49.949
If I go to hell for what I
did all those years ago,


00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:51.717
so be it.


00:15:51.718 --> 00:15:53.986
I obeyed my father.


00:15:53.987 --> 00:15:59.325
- Jacob, I have kept my
silence for 17 years.


00:15:59.326 --> 00:16:02.962
I kept my word to
Mom and Dad too.


00:16:02.963 --> 00:16:05.030
If we go to hell,


00:16:05.031 --> 00:16:06.966
it won't be for what we did.


00:16:06.967 --> 00:16:10.501
It'll be for not stopping an
evil man from killing again.


00:16:15.407 --> 00:16:17.977
This is a bad idea.


00:16:17.978 --> 00:16:20.211
The mill's been shut
down for years.


00:16:21.213 --> 00:16:22.981
We have to do this, Jacob.


00:16:39.198 --> 00:16:42.134
- Our job on this earth
is to forgive, Katie.


00:16:42.135 --> 00:16:46.238
Forgive even murder,


00:16:46.239 --> 00:16:47.405
even worse.


00:17:18.704 --> 00:17:20.739
What is it?


00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:23.408
- That rise.
- You see it?


00:17:29.415 --> 00:17:31.083
What are you doing?


00:17:31.084 --> 00:17:32.450
I'm gonna dig.


00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:57.676
It's a dog.


00:17:57.677 --> 00:17:59.545
- I'm done with this.
- Jacob.


00:17:59.546 --> 00:18:01.280
No, I'm finished.


00:18:01.281 --> 00:18:03.115
I shouldn't have come here.


00:18:03.116 --> 00:18:05.450
I shouldn't even be
speaking with you.


00:18:27.372 --> 00:18:29.108
Hey, boys.


00:18:29.109 --> 00:18:30.208
You hungry?


00:18:37.116 --> 00:18:39.150
Hello, Lucas.


00:18:41.587 --> 00:18:43.121
Katie.


00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:49.128
Thought that was you.


00:18:49.129 --> 00:18:50.262
Hmm?


00:18:50.263 --> 00:18:52.131
I saw you a few weeks ago


00:18:52.132 --> 00:18:54.166
on birch road.


00:18:54.167 --> 00:18:57.569
- Oh.


00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:58.537
I saw you too.


00:18:58.538 --> 00:18:59.571
I, um...


00:18:59.572 --> 00:19:01.305
Wasn't sure you'd recognize me.


00:19:03.909 --> 00:19:06.311
Your face...


00:19:06.312 --> 00:19:08.513
Is the same.


00:19:09.715 --> 00:19:10.849
So why are you here?


00:19:10.850 --> 00:19:12.183
What do you want?


00:19:14.319 --> 00:19:16.320
- I need to ask you
about Daniel Lapp.


00:19:18.891 --> 00:19:21.793
After 17 years of silence,


00:19:21.794 --> 00:19:23.327
Daniel Lapp.


00:19:26.199 --> 00:19:29.501
What do you want to know?


00:19:29.502 --> 00:19:32.170
- Has anyone heard from
him since he disappeared?


00:19:37.509 --> 00:19:41.213
I know you're angry with me.


00:19:41.214 --> 00:19:44.415
I think you should leave.


00:19:49.288 --> 00:19:50.489
If it's any comfort,


00:19:50.490 --> 00:19:52.324
I lived with what
I did every day.


00:19:52.325 --> 00:19:53.425
Oh, that's interesting.


00:19:53.426 --> 00:19:55.527
I lived with it too.


00:19:55.528 --> 00:19:57.228
I still do.


00:19:58.397 --> 00:19:59.798
- I don't expect
you to understand,


00:19:59.799 --> 00:20:02.201
but I, um, lost a lot too.


00:20:02.202 --> 00:20:03.635
I know what you lost:


00:20:03.636 --> 00:20:07.673
Your family, your future...


00:20:07.674 --> 00:20:09.440
Our future.


00:20:12.211 --> 00:20:15.981
- You have every
right to hate me.


00:20:15.982 --> 00:20:18.217
I don't hate anyone.


00:20:18.218 --> 00:20:21.220
It's not our way.


00:20:21.221 --> 00:20:23.555
Or have you forgotten that too?


00:20:23.556 --> 00:20:26.224
I haven't forgotten anything.


00:20:28.393 --> 00:20:31.396
I'm investigating a murder.


00:20:31.397 --> 00:20:33.665
- The girl they found yesterday?
- Yeah.


00:20:33.666 --> 00:20:36.235
- What does Daniel Lapp
have to do with that?


00:20:36.236 --> 00:20:37.302
I don't know.


00:20:37.303 --> 00:20:38.437
Just...


00:20:38.438 --> 00:20:40.338
Has anyone heard from him?


00:20:45.477 --> 00:20:46.877
If I tell you, you'll leave?


00:20:50.949 --> 00:20:52.818
If that's what you want.


00:20:52.819 --> 00:20:56.822
I think it would be best.


00:20:56.823 --> 00:21:00.291
I don't have any room for
you in my life anymore.


00:21:01.294 --> 00:21:03.562
I'm married.


00:21:03.563 --> 00:21:05.264
I know.


00:21:05.265 --> 00:21:06.565
I have children.


00:21:06.566 --> 00:21:10.435
- I know.
- I saw them.


00:21:10.436 --> 00:21:12.770
They're beautiful.


00:21:14.906 --> 00:21:16.975
No one's heard from him,


00:21:16.976 --> 00:21:18.944
not in all these years.


00:21:18.945 --> 00:21:21.279
Left without a word.


00:21:24.283 --> 00:21:26.050
It happens more than we'd wish.


00:21:41.301 --> 00:21:42.834
Do we know the age?


00:21:42.835 --> 00:21:44.303
- Can you give us a
statement, please?


00:21:44.304 --> 00:21:45.703
Do we have any suspects?


00:21:48.341 --> 00:21:49.541
Morning, chief.


00:21:49.542 --> 00:21:52.311
Messages?


00:21:52.312 --> 00:21:53.478
Oh, and, um,


00:21:53.479 --> 00:21:55.313
there's someone in your office.


00:22:03.055 --> 00:22:04.356
Can I help you?


00:22:04.357 --> 00:22:05.856
- Well, I don't know.
- Can you?


00:22:07.025 --> 00:22:08.026
You are?


00:22:08.027 --> 00:22:10.962
- Tomasetti, bci.


00:22:10.963 --> 00:22:12.497
You rang.


00:22:12.498 --> 00:22:14.399
- You ordinarily make
yourself at home


00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:15.600
in other people's offices?


00:22:15.601 --> 00:22:17.402
- Thank you.
- Mm.


00:22:17.403 --> 00:22:20.038
Well, I don't ordinarily
do a damn thing,


00:22:20.039 --> 00:22:22.507
but if you want to review
your case with me,


00:22:22.508 --> 00:22:25.609
I can offer you the benefits
of my dazzling insights.


00:22:28.348 --> 00:22:29.881
Why don't you have a seat...


00:22:29.882 --> 00:22:32.884
Kate?


00:22:32.885 --> 00:22:35.020
- How about you call
me chief burkholder?


00:22:35.021 --> 00:22:36.788
- Yeah, sure.
- Whatever you say, chief.


00:22:36.789 --> 00:22:38.857
Hey, Kate.


00:22:38.858 --> 00:22:42.361
Sheriff, hey.


00:22:42.362 --> 00:22:44.363
- Bci?
- Yeah.


00:22:44.364 --> 00:22:45.530
Nate detrick.


00:22:45.531 --> 00:22:47.999
- Yeah, tomasetti.
- We've met.


00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:49.401
- Oh, yeah?
- Where?


00:22:49.402 --> 00:22:51.136
- Last summer at
your swearing in.


00:22:51.137 --> 00:22:53.805
- Oh, right.
- Yeah, great speech.


00:22:53.806 --> 00:22:55.907
War stories.


00:22:55.908 --> 00:22:58.677
- Yeah, he was a state
trooper in Alaska.


00:22:58.678 --> 00:22:59.811
Hey, tell me.


00:22:59.812 --> 00:23:01.380
That thing you
said, is it true?


00:23:01.381 --> 00:23:03.582
You actually killed a bear?


00:23:03.583 --> 00:23:05.150
- Well...


00:23:05.151 --> 00:23:07.486
I mean, it was in
the line of duty.


00:23:07.487 --> 00:23:09.421
It was either him or me, so...


00:23:09.422 --> 00:23:10.722
Didn't want to get shot,


00:23:10.723 --> 00:23:12.391
it shouldn't have come
down to the station.


00:23:12.392 --> 00:23:13.725
- Oh, yeah, yeah.
- Right, right.


00:23:13.726 --> 00:23:16.061
That's the line I remember...


00:23:16.062 --> 00:23:17.429
station... with you.


00:23:17.430 --> 00:23:18.496
That's funny.


00:23:20.699 --> 00:23:23.468
- Um, Kate, um...


00:23:23.469 --> 00:23:24.936
Did the mayor call?


00:23:24.937 --> 00:23:25.937
This morning?


00:23:25.938 --> 00:23:27.672
Um...


00:23:27.673 --> 00:23:28.707
Yeah, three times.


00:23:28.708 --> 00:23:29.808
Why?


00:23:29.809 --> 00:23:31.109
- Is that why you're here?
- No, no.


00:23:31.110 --> 00:23:33.145
I mean, I was... I was
gonna drop by anyway.


00:23:33.146 --> 00:23:35.714
- He wants your office to
take over the investigation?


00:23:35.715 --> 00:23:36.782
No, no, no.


00:23:36.783 --> 00:23:38.650
I-I set him straight on that.


00:23:38.651 --> 00:23:40.552
Um, I just wanted
to let you know


00:23:40.553 --> 00:23:42.554
that if you need the county
to do anything for you,


00:23:42.555 --> 00:23:44.656
run some legwork, just,
you know, let me know.


00:23:44.657 --> 00:23:47.092
- I'm there for you.
- Okay, Nate.


00:23:47.093 --> 00:23:48.827
I appreciate that.


00:23:48.828 --> 00:23:50.429
You got it.


00:23:50.430 --> 00:23:52.731
Is there a file ready?


00:23:52.732 --> 00:23:54.032
Of course there are.


00:23:54.033 --> 00:23:55.567
You can get Mona to make
some copies for you.


00:23:55.568 --> 00:23:57.002
- Auggie.
- Morning, sheriff.


00:23:57.003 --> 00:23:58.470
- Um...
- You got a minute?


00:23:58.471 --> 00:23:59.738
Yup.


00:23:59.739 --> 00:24:02.174
- Um, auggie, this is
John tomasetti, bci.


00:24:02.175 --> 00:24:03.475
- Ah!
- The mayor.


00:24:03.476 --> 00:24:05.710
- Glad you're here.
- Thanks.


00:24:05.711 --> 00:24:06.878
So, Kate, uh,


00:24:06.879 --> 00:24:07.979
the town Council would like


00:24:07.980 --> 00:24:09.080
all public statements


00:24:09.081 --> 00:24:10.482
on this situation we're having


00:24:10.483 --> 00:24:11.564
to be cleared through them.


00:24:12.819 --> 00:24:14.052
Seriously? Why?


00:24:14.053 --> 00:24:16.054
- Well, they feel that
it's taken a long time


00:24:16.055 --> 00:24:17.456
to develop the tourism here...


00:24:17.457 --> 00:24:18.790
- tourism?
- That's their concern?


00:24:18.791 --> 00:24:20.659
They're not more concerned
about catching the...


00:24:20.660 --> 00:24:22.828
- Kate, all public statements
will be cleared through them


00:24:22.829 --> 00:24:23.995
until further notice.


00:24:23.996 --> 00:24:25.030
Now, if you have an
issue with this...


00:24:25.031 --> 00:24:26.498
I certainly do have an issue.


00:24:26.499 --> 00:24:28.166
- Kate, your attitude,
it's not helping.


00:24:28.167 --> 00:24:29.501
Okay? It's not helping here.


00:24:29.502 --> 00:24:30.669
Now, you were hired


00:24:30.670 --> 00:24:31.870
because of your
special sensitivity


00:24:31.871 --> 00:24:33.505
to the dual nature
of our community.


00:24:33.506 --> 00:24:34.873
We value our amish citizens


00:24:34.874 --> 00:24:36.641
and not just because of the
revenue they bring us.


00:24:36.642 --> 00:24:37.976
But we did not think
for a moment...


00:24:37.977 --> 00:24:39.978
- what, that I would have
anything important to do?


00:24:39.979 --> 00:24:42.147
- Oh, Kate, that is nonsense.
- Really, auggie?


00:24:42.148 --> 00:24:44.182
- Yes, you are being...
- Whoa, whoa, auggie.


00:24:44.183 --> 00:24:46.485
Auggie, let's go grab a
cup of coffee, my friend.


00:24:46.486 --> 00:24:47.686
I'm buying.


00:24:47.687 --> 00:24:49.087
I'm sure Kate understands
the situation


00:24:49.088 --> 00:24:50.522
a little better than we do.


00:24:50.523 --> 00:24:52.791
Come on.


00:24:52.792 --> 00:24:55.093
Come on.


00:24:55.094 --> 00:24:56.261
- Very good to meet you.
- Yeah.


00:24:56.262 --> 00:24:57.728
No, that was great.


00:25:04.503 --> 00:25:06.972
There's no smoking in here.


00:25:06.973 --> 00:25:08.506
Bad night?


00:25:11.009 --> 00:25:13.945
These are the cold cases.


00:25:13.946 --> 00:25:15.546
Terrific.


00:25:40.305 --> 00:25:43.074
They all like this?


00:25:43.075 --> 00:25:45.810
Yeah, just like that.


00:25:45.811 --> 00:25:47.311
You feel like helping,
put that out.


00:26:00.825 --> 00:26:03.061
- Yup, she put up a
hell of a fight.


00:26:03.062 --> 00:26:05.130
From the ligature marks
on her wrists and ankles,


00:26:05.131 --> 00:26:07.232
she may even have broken
free a few times.


00:26:07.233 --> 00:26:09.701
- How long you think he
might have had with her?


00:26:09.702 --> 00:26:11.303
- Some of these cuts
are partially healed,


00:26:11.304 --> 00:26:13.572
so I'd say...


00:26:13.573 --> 00:26:16.041
A week at least,
probably more.


00:26:16.042 --> 00:26:17.742
I wish these people


00:26:17.743 --> 00:26:20.345
would be a little less reluctant
to report somebody missing.


00:26:20.346 --> 00:26:23.048
Yeah, well, these people


00:26:23.049 --> 00:26:25.283
like to take care of
their own problems.


00:26:25.284 --> 00:26:27.285
- Look. I'm sorry.
- Kate, I didn't mean it that way.


00:26:27.286 --> 00:26:29.921
- No, it's okay.
- You're right.


00:26:29.922 --> 00:26:31.122
The police didn't know.


00:26:31.123 --> 00:26:33.058
I'd been gone for
almost six months.


00:26:33.059 --> 00:26:34.758
- Huh.
- Police are English.


00:26:36.628 --> 00:26:37.929
Hey.


00:26:37.930 --> 00:26:39.064
- Hey, you get
through the files?


00:26:39.065 --> 00:26:40.365
Yeah, I'll give you


00:26:40.366 --> 00:26:43.301
a General profile of
the guy by tomorrow.


00:26:43.302 --> 00:26:46.271
But a couple of things
pop for me right off.


00:26:46.272 --> 00:26:49.608
All right.


00:26:49.609 --> 00:26:52.110
There's no DNA anywhere,


00:26:52.111 --> 00:26:55.880
no fluids, hair, or
skin flakes, nothing.


00:26:55.881 --> 00:26:57.115
Yeah, nothing here either.


00:26:57.116 --> 00:26:58.383
Right, so he's either


00:26:58.384 --> 00:27:01.252
the luckiest serial
killer on record, or...


00:27:01.253 --> 00:27:04.055
- he scrubbed down
the body postmortem.


00:27:04.056 --> 00:27:07.125
- The question is, why'd
he start up again?


00:27:07.126 --> 00:27:09.094
You know, there's five
dead girls in the '90s.


00:27:09.095 --> 00:27:11.796
He stops. Now he's back.


00:27:11.797 --> 00:27:14.131
What's got him going?


00:27:16.034 --> 00:27:17.635
Any thoughts, Kate?


00:27:22.107 --> 00:27:23.308
He's a copycat.


00:27:23.309 --> 00:27:25.210
- No, no, the Roman
numeral thing,


00:27:25.211 --> 00:27:27.012
I mean, that was
never made public.


00:27:27.013 --> 00:27:28.313
- Yeah, that could
have been leaked.


00:27:28.314 --> 00:27:30.148
Dozens of people
read that case file.


00:27:30.149 --> 00:27:31.683
Well...


00:27:31.684 --> 00:27:32.751
- that file was sitting
in an unlocked cabinet


00:27:32.752 --> 00:27:33.985
for 17 years.


00:27:33.986 --> 00:27:35.053
You can't tell me...


00:27:35.054 --> 00:27:36.354
- Chief?
- Hey.


00:27:36.355 --> 00:27:38.123
Did skid get to the bishop?


00:27:38.124 --> 00:27:40.291
Yeah, um...


00:27:40.292 --> 00:27:44.295
Ezra and Bonnie ausberger.


00:27:44.296 --> 00:27:47.165
I know who they are.


00:27:47.166 --> 00:27:48.433
They got a teenage daughter


00:27:48.434 --> 00:27:51.135
who's been missing a
little over two weeks.


00:27:58.943 --> 00:28:01.111
Hello, ezra, Bonnie.


00:28:48.359 --> 00:28:51.396
- When was the last time
they saw their daughter?


00:28:51.397 --> 00:28:54.065
- When was the last time
you saw your daughter?


00:28:54.066 --> 00:28:57.001
Two weeks ago, Sunday.


00:28:57.002 --> 00:29:00.371
She said she was going to
her work after services.


00:29:00.372 --> 00:29:02.040
She worked on the sabbath?


00:29:02.041 --> 00:29:04.242
- She worked on the sabbath?


00:29:04.243 --> 00:29:05.977
She takes care of the babies


00:29:05.978 --> 00:29:09.114
so their mothers can go
to afternoon service.


00:29:09.115 --> 00:29:11.216
- And she didn't
show up that day?


00:29:11.217 --> 00:29:12.884
And she didn't show...


00:29:12.885 --> 00:29:14.519
no.


00:29:14.520 --> 00:29:19.357
- Why didn't you inform
the police before now?


00:29:19.358 --> 00:29:23.528
- Our daughter had
become unruly.


00:29:23.529 --> 00:29:25.830
We thought she had run away.


00:29:25.831 --> 00:29:27.432
- It's not a matter
for the police.


00:29:27.433 --> 00:29:30.769
That's an amish matter.


00:29:30.770 --> 00:29:32.871
We went to the bishop.


00:29:32.872 --> 00:29:35.105
I understand.


00:29:36.407 --> 00:29:37.776
We want to take


00:29:37.777 --> 00:29:39.443
our daughter now.


00:29:42.247 --> 00:29:44.883
We want to bring her home.


00:29:44.884 --> 00:29:48.452
- I'm afraid we can't
let you take her yet.


00:29:50.956 --> 00:29:52.089
Sorry.


00:30:08.473 --> 00:30:10.275
- All right, what
the hell was that?


00:30:10.276 --> 00:30:11.876
Just what it looked like.


00:30:11.877 --> 00:30:13.511
- Well, it looks like they're
not speaking to you.


00:30:13.512 --> 00:30:15.814
- Why?
- Because I left.


00:30:15.815 --> 00:30:17.982
- Yeah, I'm sorry.
- I should have put that together.


00:30:17.983 --> 00:30:19.918
- You're amish.
- Yes.


00:30:19.919 --> 00:30:21.186
Well, what happened?


00:30:21.187 --> 00:30:22.554
You want my life story?


00:30:22.555 --> 00:30:24.322
- I'd settle for how you
ended up back here.


00:30:24.323 --> 00:30:26.291
There was a job.


00:30:26.292 --> 00:30:27.859
That's all I get?


00:30:27.860 --> 00:30:29.594
- I grew up here, left at 18,


00:30:29.595 --> 00:30:31.329
waitressed in
Cleveland for a year,


00:30:31.330 --> 00:30:32.897
hated it,


00:30:32.898 --> 00:30:35.300
went to school, took the
police exam, passed,


00:30:35.301 --> 00:30:37.135
made detective at 28.


00:30:37.136 --> 00:30:38.336
I applied for the
job here last year


00:30:38.337 --> 00:30:39.404
when chief mackie retired.


00:30:39.405 --> 00:30:40.939
Are we good now?


00:30:40.940 --> 00:30:43.241
Oh, man. I'm so glad.


00:30:43.242 --> 00:30:45.476
Yeah, why is that?


00:30:45.477 --> 00:30:46.845
No, it's just I thought


00:30:46.846 --> 00:30:48.913
you were one of
those horrible...


00:30:48.914 --> 00:30:51.315
You know, boring...


00:30:53.184 --> 00:30:55.386
But you're a stiff
because you're amish.


00:30:55.387 --> 00:30:56.588
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.


00:30:56.589 --> 00:30:58.156
Chief!


00:30:58.157 --> 00:31:00.959
Uh, bishop gave me something
to pass on to you.


00:31:00.960 --> 00:31:03.327
He said someone slipped it
under his door this morning.


00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:10.602
What's it say?


00:31:10.603 --> 00:31:12.436
What's it say, Kate?


00:31:13.505 --> 00:31:15.373
It says, uh,


00:31:15.374 --> 00:31:18.877
"Katie burkholder knows
who the killer is."


00:31:18.878 --> 00:31:20.645
Someone's idea of a joke.


00:31:20.646 --> 00:31:23.413
- I wasn't aware the amish
were into that kind of humor.


00:31:25.984 --> 00:31:27.385
You got things to do, right?


00:31:27.386 --> 00:31:28.386
Hmm?


00:31:28.387 --> 00:31:29.887
Oh, sure.


00:31:31.356 --> 00:31:32.457
Do you have a problem?


00:31:32.458 --> 00:31:33.658
Yeah, something's going on,


00:31:33.659 --> 00:31:36.394
and you're not
letting me in on it.


00:31:36.395 --> 00:31:39.097
It's okay, 'cause
whatever it is,


00:31:39.098 --> 00:31:41.398
it's not gonna stay
a secret forong.


00:32:03.988 --> 00:32:05.990
You're back.


00:32:05.991 --> 00:32:09.226
- I'm sorry.
- I... Need your help.


00:32:10.528 --> 00:32:12.363
Again?


00:32:12.364 --> 00:32:16.434
- Someone wrote a letter
to the bishop about me.


00:32:16.435 --> 00:32:18.269
I need to know who.


00:32:18.270 --> 00:32:20.203
What are you asking me to do?


00:32:22.240 --> 00:32:23.541
Go to him?


00:32:23.542 --> 00:32:25.410
The bishop?


00:32:25.411 --> 00:32:27.244
You know he won't talk to me.


00:32:32.518 --> 00:32:35.585
Does this have something
to do with Daniel Lapp?


00:32:36.989 --> 00:32:38.423
- I'm sorry.
- I can't tell you that.


00:32:38.424 --> 00:32:41.092
It's important?


00:32:41.093 --> 00:32:44.195
Yeah.


00:32:44.196 --> 00:32:48.366
I would tell you if I could.


00:32:48.367 --> 00:32:51.101
- It's not like you
to hold your tongue.


00:32:53.571 --> 00:32:55.305
No.


00:32:56.308 --> 00:32:58.308
It's not.


00:33:03.314 --> 00:33:07.317
I can't promise the bishop
will tell me anything.


00:33:08.454 --> 00:33:11.121
But I want to know
something first.


00:33:13.057 --> 00:33:14.125
All right.


00:33:14.126 --> 00:33:16.728
I want to know what happened.


00:33:16.729 --> 00:33:19.230
Why did you leave?


00:33:19.231 --> 00:33:21.465
Chief, what's your 20?


00:33:26.304 --> 00:33:28.072
On patrol.


00:33:28.073 --> 00:33:30.240
We got a hit from drc.


00:33:32.477 --> 00:33:33.611
Suspect?


00:33:33.612 --> 00:33:35.279
How fast can you get here?


00:33:35.280 --> 00:33:39.350
We're at 721 Ridge road.


00:33:39.351 --> 00:33:41.318
- On my way.
- Ten minutes.


00:33:48.693 --> 00:33:50.528
I didn't want to.


00:33:50.529 --> 00:33:53.498
Then why?


00:33:53.499 --> 00:33:55.366
It wasn't my choice.


00:33:55.367 --> 00:33:56.767
Then whose?


00:34:00.772 --> 00:34:02.339
Lucas, I can't tell you.


00:34:04.776 --> 00:34:06.576
I can't.


00:34:32.805 --> 00:34:35.673
- An ex-con named Wayne
starkie, a rapist.


00:34:35.674 --> 00:34:37.408
He worked the
slaughterhouse in prison,


00:34:37.409 --> 00:34:39.209
has a thing for knives.


00:34:40.411 --> 00:34:41.779
Go around to the back.


00:34:41.780 --> 00:34:44.081
Key your walkie when you
get to the back door.


00:34:51.389 --> 00:34:52.590
Mr. starkie?


00:34:52.591 --> 00:34:53.691
Yeah. Who is it?


00:34:53.692 --> 00:34:54.659
Painters mill pd.


00:34:54.660 --> 00:34:55.693
Open the door.


00:34:55.694 --> 00:34:57.328
- No way.
- Open up.


00:34:57.329 --> 00:34:59.197
Go away.


00:34:59.198 --> 00:35:01.165
Mr. starkie!


00:35:01.166 --> 00:35:03.634
Hey, what are you doing?


00:35:03.635 --> 00:35:04.802
- Hey!
- Tomasetti?


00:35:04.803 --> 00:35:06.804
- Whoa!


00:35:06.805 --> 00:35:09.107
Get down on the ground.


00:35:09.108 --> 00:35:10.408
I said stay down.


00:35:10.409 --> 00:35:11.742
- Son of a bitch!
- Stay down.


00:35:11.743 --> 00:35:14.445
Get off of me.


00:35:14.446 --> 00:35:15.545
- Stay down.
- Get off me.


00:35:16.715 --> 00:35:18.549
Tomasetti.


00:35:18.550 --> 00:35:20.785
- What?
- You see the blood?


00:35:20.786 --> 00:35:23.454
- There's a joint on the table.
- Oh, it's tobacco, man.


00:35:23.455 --> 00:35:25.122
- Yeah?
- It looks like a joint to me.


00:35:26.657 --> 00:35:27.725
- Come on. Stand up.
- Ugh!


00:35:27.726 --> 00:35:31.461
- Stand up. Stand up.
- I said...


00:35:34.199 --> 00:35:36.367
Oh! Oh.


00:35:36.368 --> 00:35:37.435
- Sit down.


00:35:37.436 --> 00:35:39.837
Nichols. Nichols!


00:35:39.838 --> 00:35:41.439
Get in here.


00:35:41.440 --> 00:35:43.608
Hold him.


00:35:43.609 --> 00:35:45.643
- Where you been the last week?
- Here.


00:35:45.644 --> 00:35:47.245
Can anyone back that up?


00:35:47.246 --> 00:35:49.447
- What do I need an alibi for?
- For what?


00:35:49.448 --> 00:35:51.415
Back it up!


00:35:51.416 --> 00:35:52.483
Okay, look.


00:35:52.484 --> 00:35:54.752
I went hunting with my brother.


00:35:54.753 --> 00:35:55.920
Take him in.


00:35:55.921 --> 00:35:57.688
- What for?
- I just told you.


00:35:57.689 --> 00:35:59.490
- Possession of a firearm.
- You're on parole.


00:35:59.491 --> 00:36:01.492
What'd you do, forget?


00:36:01.493 --> 00:36:02.894
- I didn't do nothing!
- Come on!


00:36:02.895 --> 00:36:05.695
- Secure the weapon.
- Come on!


00:36:08.333 --> 00:36:09.600
- Okay, first of all,
just to be clear,


00:36:09.601 --> 00:36:11.169
that never happens again.


00:36:11.170 --> 00:36:12.637
- What, you wanted to wait
for him to let us in?


00:36:12.638 --> 00:36:14.405
- You broke half a
dozen laws in there,


00:36:14.406 --> 00:36:16.240
not to mention he's not
our guy, and you know it.


00:36:16.241 --> 00:36:17.808
Do I?


00:36:17.809 --> 00:36:19.544
- Dirty dishes,
dirty fingernails,


00:36:19.545 --> 00:36:21.312
smokes, drinks, trips
on his shoelaces.


00:36:21.313 --> 00:36:22.346
What is wrong with you?


00:36:22.347 --> 00:36:24.482
I'm fine.


00:36:24.483 --> 00:36:26.384
No, you're not.


00:36:26.385 --> 00:36:28.852
I just need a drink.


00:36:32.858 --> 00:36:35.492
That's how it is right now every
time the adrenaline hits.


00:36:36.728 --> 00:36:39.397
- PTSD.
- Yeah, something like that.


00:36:39.398 --> 00:36:40.431
You need a doctor?


00:36:40.432 --> 00:36:42.599
No, just a drink.


00:36:44.635 --> 00:36:46.536
- Why are you still
on active duty?


00:36:48.240 --> 00:36:49.540
'Cause I'm brilliant
at this stuff.


00:36:49.541 --> 00:36:50.607
Can't you tell?


00:36:57.949 --> 00:37:00.318
I-I know I shouldn't be here.


00:37:00.319 --> 00:37:01.519
So retire.


00:37:01.520 --> 00:37:03.554
- Yeah, well, I, uh...


00:37:03.555 --> 00:37:05.789
I don't do too well at home.


00:37:08.392 --> 00:37:10.595
They took pity on
me at the office.


00:37:10.596 --> 00:37:14.365
They said I could hang there
until the new captain showed up.


00:37:14.366 --> 00:37:15.833
But, uh, slaughterhouse
showed up first,


00:37:15.834 --> 00:37:18.401
so here I am.


00:37:19.437 --> 00:37:23.541
What happened to you?


00:37:23.542 --> 00:37:26.410
- You heard of me.
- I'm tomasetti.


00:37:26.411 --> 00:37:29.547
Tomasetti, Cincinnati.


00:37:29.548 --> 00:37:33.017
It was in all the papers.


00:37:33.018 --> 00:37:35.586
All right, I wanted to
make a name for myself


00:37:35.587 --> 00:37:36.988
when I made detective,


00:37:36.989 --> 00:37:39.357
so when I got my shield, I
took down Joey campanella.


00:37:39.358 --> 00:37:41.459
Does that ring a Bell?


00:37:41.460 --> 00:37:42.727
- Yeah, okay.
- I remember that.


00:37:42.728 --> 00:37:45.528
- Yeah.
- Godfather to half of Ohio.


00:37:46.764 --> 00:37:48.299
He said he would
get even with me,


00:37:48.300 --> 00:37:50.401
and I knew that he would try,


00:37:50.402 --> 00:37:53.704
so I wore kevlar every day.


00:37:53.705 --> 00:37:57.608
But he faked me out.


00:37:57.609 --> 00:37:59.542
He didn't go after me.


00:38:04.682 --> 00:38:06.884
He went after your family.


00:38:06.885 --> 00:38:08.886
Yeah, my wife


00:38:08.887 --> 00:38:11.589
and, um...


00:38:11.590 --> 00:38:13.590
My kid.


00:38:16.061 --> 00:38:18.428
They never made an
arrest for that.


00:38:25.636 --> 00:38:27.470
- Get me another.
- Coming right up.


00:38:29.440 --> 00:38:32.777
I'm sorry.


00:38:32.778 --> 00:38:34.912
- I made sure I was
first in the door


00:38:34.913 --> 00:38:36.514
for about five
years after that.


00:38:36.515 --> 00:38:38.649
You know, there was
every high-speed chase,


00:38:38.650 --> 00:38:42.019
shootout, hostage situation.


00:38:42.020 --> 00:38:43.621
I was there.


00:38:43.622 --> 00:38:45.389
Trying to get yourself killed?


00:38:45.390 --> 00:38:48.592
Something like that.


00:38:48.593 --> 00:38:49.993
But it didn't work.
I'm still here.


00:38:53.465 --> 00:38:55.065
What's left of me.


00:38:58.636 --> 00:38:59.804
Okay, look, I won't blame you


00:38:59.805 --> 00:39:00.938
if you don't believe a word


00:39:00.939 --> 00:39:02.340
that I have to say
about this case,


00:39:02.341 --> 00:39:03.407
but I know one thing:


00:39:03.408 --> 00:39:04.642
This is not a copycat.


00:39:04.643 --> 00:39:06.010
Based on what?


00:39:06.011 --> 00:39:07.545
- Everything: The
Roman numerals,


00:39:07.546 --> 00:39:08.646
the cuts to the carotid artery.


00:39:08.647 --> 00:39:09.680
They're all scrubbed.


00:39:09.681 --> 00:39:10.948
I mean, a copycat would need


00:39:10.949 --> 00:39:14.618
a set of instructions
with him each time.


00:39:14.619 --> 00:39:16.387
So what does the
FBI have to say?


00:39:16.388 --> 00:39:19.123
- We've got the vcap file,
and there's not much there.


00:39:19.124 --> 00:39:22.059
- Yeah, well, my gut says he's
been all over the country.


00:39:22.060 --> 00:39:24.362
- Because of the gap
in the numbers?


00:39:24.363 --> 00:39:28.466
I looked. I looked.
Nothing much is up.


00:39:28.467 --> 00:39:30.667
Chief, we need you now.


00:39:36.640 --> 00:39:38.676
- Excuse me, please.
- Skid.


00:39:38.677 --> 00:39:39.710
What's going on, here?


00:39:39.711 --> 00:39:41.879
Uh, parents. Gymnastics meet.


00:39:41.880 --> 00:39:44.514
- Starting when?
- Don't know. Ten minutes ago?


00:39:48.953 --> 00:39:50.988
No.


00:39:50.989 --> 00:39:53.457
- Oh, no.
- Kate.


00:39:53.458 --> 00:39:55.693
- He's escalating.
- Tell me about it.


00:39:55.694 --> 00:39:57.395
- T.J.!
- Now, hold on.


00:39:57.396 --> 00:39:59.029
He did this so he can
watch these people react.


00:39:59.030 --> 00:40:00.398
He's here.


00:40:00.399 --> 00:40:01.766
I know it doesn't
match his m.O.,


00:40:01.767 --> 00:40:03.100
but it's dead-on
for his profile.


00:40:03.101 --> 00:40:04.468
He's here.


00:40:04.469 --> 00:40:05.669
Is the mayor on his way?


00:40:05.670 --> 00:40:07.138
- Yeah, he's outside.
- Keep him there.


00:40:07.139 --> 00:40:09.807
- What do I say to him?
- Just do it.


00:40:09.808 --> 00:40:12.610
Skid, lock the doors.
No one leaves.


00:40:12.611 --> 00:40:14.678
Nichols, anyone within
200 yards of here,


00:40:14.679 --> 00:40:16.080
bring them inside,
no exceptions.


00:40:16.081 --> 00:40:17.948
And I want all number plates
within a mile of here.


00:40:17.949 --> 00:40:19.717
Got it, chief.


00:40:19.718 --> 00:40:21.719
- What's going on?
- He's here.


00:40:21.720 --> 00:40:23.953
- Who?
- The killer. He's here.


00:40:30.694 --> 00:40:31.762
Nobody leaves this place.


00:40:31.763 --> 00:40:33.497
I want to set up a perimeter.


00:40:33.498 --> 00:40:35.533
Nobody leaves this building.


00:40:35.534 --> 00:40:38.169
Stay outside?


00:40:38.170 --> 00:40:39.570
- Kate! Kate!
- Auggie. Auggie.


00:40:39.571 --> 00:40:40.971
- Please let me know.
- Auggie, please.


00:40:40.972 --> 00:40:42.907
I need to ask you to back
off for another second.


00:40:42.908 --> 00:40:45.008
Just stay here for one second.
We just need...


00:40:46.010 --> 00:40:47.511
Auggie.


00:40:47.512 --> 00:40:50.514
Oh, my God.


00:40:50.515 --> 00:40:51.982
Oh, my God. No, no, no.


00:40:51.983 --> 00:40:54.652
Oh, my God.


00:40:54.653 --> 00:40:56.454
- Oh, God, Amanda. Honey.
- Auggie. Auggie, please.


00:40:56.455 --> 00:40:58.456
- We need to... you can't right now.
- Get away from me. Get away.


00:40:58.457 --> 00:41:01.659
Get away from me!


00:41:01.660 --> 00:41:04.762
Look what he did to my daughter.


00:41:04.763 --> 00:41:06.063
- Auggie, no.
- Honey, no.


00:41:06.064 --> 00:41:09.500
- Oh, God.
- Hey, hey, hey.


00:41:09.501 --> 00:41:10.768
Come on, auggie. She's gone.


00:41:10.769 --> 00:41:11.902
No, no, no, no, no.


00:41:11.903 --> 00:41:12.803
- Come on.
- Let us do our job.


00:41:12.804 --> 00:41:14.772
- No, no!
- Please, let me...


00:41:14.773 --> 00:41:16.506
no, please!


00:41:27.117 --> 00:41:29.053
- There are no more details
provided at this time.


00:41:29.054 --> 00:41:31.989
We are waiting for a statement.


00:41:31.990 --> 00:41:33.958
- I want to know why we're
being treated like criminals.


00:41:33.959 --> 00:41:35.726
Please, just bear with us.


00:41:35.727 --> 00:41:38.028
You'll get to go home as soon
as everyone's been processed.


00:41:38.029 --> 00:41:40.164
- I realize this isn't what you
people want to do right now.


00:41:40.165 --> 00:41:42.032
- Just hang in there.
- Your killer isn't here.


00:41:42.033 --> 00:41:44.235
You know as well as I
do the killer's amish.


00:41:44.236 --> 00:41:46.637
- Every one of them
knows how to butcher.


00:41:46.638 --> 00:41:48.138
They slaughter animals
in their backyard.


00:41:48.139 --> 00:41:50.741
- Mr. waring, I need
you to calm down.


00:41:50.742 --> 00:41:51.775
Well, they do.


00:41:51.776 --> 00:41:52.742
No, sir, they don't.


00:41:54.946 --> 00:41:55.913
Yeah?


00:41:55.914 --> 00:41:56.881
FBI's on line two,


00:41:56.882 --> 00:41:57.915
returning your call.


00:41:57.916 --> 00:41:59.517
Great. Give me a sec.


00:41:59.518 --> 00:42:02.019
- All right, I'll
handle the natives.


00:42:02.020 --> 00:42:04.722
Look, I'll get you out of here
just as soon as possible.


00:42:04.723 --> 00:42:06.123
- Okay, I need
everything you've got:


00:42:06.124 --> 00:42:07.658
Postmortem, carved numerals,


00:42:07.659 --> 00:42:09.293
any woman killed
by exsanguination.


00:42:09.294 --> 00:42:12.630
No, anywhere, any state.


00:42:12.631 --> 00:42:13.797
Wait. You're just
doing it now?


00:42:13.798 --> 00:42:14.932
I called you two days ago.


00:42:14.933 --> 00:42:16.267
FBI?


00:42:16.268 --> 00:42:18.968
Yes! Now.


00:42:19.971 --> 00:42:21.772
Yeah, not sure you'd win


00:42:21.773 --> 00:42:23.607
a popularity
contest right now.


00:42:23.608 --> 00:42:25.676
I am aware.


00:42:25.677 --> 00:42:26.810
- So why does someone
in this town


00:42:26.811 --> 00:42:28.711
think you know who
the killer is?


00:42:29.947 --> 00:42:31.582
What?


00:42:31.583 --> 00:42:34.684
- Who wrote the
letter to the bishop?


00:42:35.921 --> 00:42:36.954
This is what you
want to talk about?


00:42:36.955 --> 00:42:39.890
Mm-hmm.


00:42:39.891 --> 00:42:42.059
It's gossip, John.


00:42:42.060 --> 00:42:43.627
The amish curse:


00:42:43.628 --> 00:42:44.828
No televisions, no radio,


00:42:44.829 --> 00:42:45.829
so they gossip.


00:42:45.830 --> 00:42:47.131
They send letters to the bishop.


00:42:47.132 --> 00:42:48.899
That's what they do.


00:42:48.900 --> 00:42:51.835
That's your answer?


00:42:51.836 --> 00:42:53.036
Yeah, that's my answer.


00:42:57.174 --> 00:42:58.776
- You know, it
might not be smart


00:42:58.777 --> 00:43:01.044
to underestimate me, Kate.


00:43:02.313 --> 00:43:03.913
I don't underestimate anyone.


00:43:11.855 --> 00:43:13.090
That national search


00:43:13.091 --> 00:43:14.892
for the slaughterhouse
killer continues.


00:43:14.893 --> 00:43:17.160
Police are releasing
no information.


00:43:50.829 --> 00:43:52.262
Katie.


00:43:52.263 --> 00:43:55.099
Sorry, I didn't mean
to frighten you.


00:43:55.100 --> 00:43:57.868
No, it's all right.


00:43:57.869 --> 00:44:00.204
What are you doing here?


00:44:00.205 --> 00:44:01.905
I've been to see your brother.


00:44:01.906 --> 00:44:04.875
He told me...


00:44:04.876 --> 00:44:07.177
About Lapp.


00:44:07.178 --> 00:44:10.047
He...


00:44:10.048 --> 00:44:13.183
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
He what... he what?


00:44:13.184 --> 00:44:15.251
What Lapp did to you, Katie.


00:44:17.921 --> 00:44:19.923
Why didn't you come to me?


00:44:19.924 --> 00:44:22.725
Why didn't you tell me?


00:44:24.095 --> 00:44:28.899
I have wanted to, Lucas.


00:44:28.900 --> 00:44:32.102
I'm so sorry I didn't.


00:44:32.103 --> 00:44:34.004
I would have stood by you.


00:44:34.005 --> 00:44:37.041
You went through this all alone.


00:44:37.042 --> 00:44:39.710
I would have done
anything for you, Katie.


00:44:39.711 --> 00:44:43.113
I know that.


00:44:43.114 --> 00:44:45.716
But you know what?
I'm all right now.


00:44:45.717 --> 00:44:47.717
It's done.


00:44:49.687 --> 00:44:52.356
It isn't, Katie.


00:44:52.357 --> 00:44:55.325
You have to go see
your brother.


00:44:55.326 --> 00:44:57.027
Why?


00:44:57.028 --> 00:45:00.264
The bishop,


00:45:00.265 --> 00:45:02.833
he doesn't know who
wrote the letter.


00:45:02.834 --> 00:45:04.968
You went to the bishop?


00:45:04.969 --> 00:45:06.737
As you asked.


00:45:06.738 --> 00:45:09.106
He said whoever did,


00:45:09.107 --> 00:45:11.175
they didn't come
by car or buggy.


00:45:11.176 --> 00:45:14.878
I figured they must have come
through his back fields.


00:45:14.879 --> 00:45:18.315
There were tracks.


00:45:18.316 --> 00:45:20.983
I followed them to
your brother's farm.


00:45:22.986 --> 00:45:25.456
That's not possible.


00:45:25.457 --> 00:45:28.925
- You asked me to
help you, Katie.


00:45:44.075 --> 00:45:45.842
I'll be right back.


00:45:47.878 --> 00:45:49.378
You missed me.


00:45:55.853 --> 00:45:56.954
Shh!


00:45:56.955 --> 00:45:59.355
Shh.


00:46:05.295 --> 00:46:06.363
What?


00:46:06.364 --> 00:46:08.030
What is it?


00:46:13.203 --> 00:46:14.538
What happened?


00:46:14.539 --> 00:46:17.241
- Did you write the
bishop about me?


00:46:17.242 --> 00:46:18.308
What?


00:46:18.309 --> 00:46:20.010
- You wrote the
bishop a letter


00:46:20.011 --> 00:46:22.146
about me and Daniel Lapp.


00:46:22.147 --> 00:46:23.547
What are you talking about?


00:46:23.548 --> 00:46:25.048
Don't lie to me, Jacob.


00:46:25.049 --> 00:46:27.050
We know it came from you.


00:46:27.051 --> 00:46:28.284
Lie to you?


00:46:47.871 --> 00:46:49.840
This is my business.


00:46:49.841 --> 00:46:50.974
I'm finished.


00:46:50.975 --> 00:46:54.344
All this silence,
it never ends.


00:46:54.345 --> 00:46:58.414
This is how you want to live?


00:47:01.052 --> 00:47:04.221
I wrote the bishop.


00:47:04.222 --> 00:47:06.590
How else can this end?


00:47:06.591 --> 00:47:08.292
I look at you.


00:47:08.293 --> 00:47:10.060
I see this thing,


00:47:10.061 --> 00:47:11.228
this terrible thing,


00:47:11.229 --> 00:47:13.497
eating at you each day.


00:47:13.498 --> 00:47:16.233
You don't see what
it's doing to him.


00:47:16.234 --> 00:47:17.835
It tortures him.


00:47:17.836 --> 00:47:19.303
- Tortures him?
- How?


00:47:19.304 --> 00:47:21.071
- Because he knows
it's torturing you.


00:47:21.072 --> 00:47:22.072
How would he know?


00:47:22.073 --> 00:47:25.142
He barely looks at me.


00:47:25.143 --> 00:47:27.110
What do you expect him to do?


00:47:27.111 --> 00:47:29.580
You're under the ban.


00:47:29.581 --> 00:47:32.216
You think he has no feelings,


00:47:32.217 --> 00:47:35.084
no love for his sister?


00:47:38.422 --> 00:47:42.192
He looks for you every morning.


00:47:42.193 --> 00:47:43.994
You don't know that?


00:47:43.995 --> 00:47:45.928
Every morning.


00:47:48.232 --> 00:47:50.600
Is that true?


00:47:59.309 --> 00:48:01.078
I remembered,


00:48:01.079 --> 00:48:04.348
when I was speaking
with Sarah,


00:48:04.349 --> 00:48:07.284
something.


00:48:07.285 --> 00:48:11.288
When Dad came home that
night, he told Mom,


00:48:11.289 --> 00:48:15.058
"I put him in the
deepest place,


00:48:15.059 --> 00:48:16.492
a place no one will
ever find him."


00:48:20.964 --> 00:48:22.465
Maybe that will help.


00:48:25.135 --> 00:48:27.103
I don't know.


00:48:40.051 --> 00:48:42.184
You know, I remember
now why I chose you.


00:48:46.223 --> 00:48:47.591
- I wasn't wrong.
- Shh.


00:48:47.592 --> 00:48:48.959
No, I was just...


00:48:48.960 --> 00:48:50.160
Katie, for once,


00:48:50.161 --> 00:48:52.929
just... Shush.


00:48:55.165 --> 00:48:56.999
You're English now.


00:50:44.641 --> 00:50:46.442
Looking for something?


00:50:48.178 --> 00:50:50.147
John.


00:50:50.148 --> 00:50:52.649
Hey, yeah, um...


00:50:52.650 --> 00:50:55.385
I got a tip on an
illegal dumping site.


00:50:55.386 --> 00:50:57.521
I thought I would
check it out.


00:50:57.522 --> 00:51:01.258
Right. Yeah.


00:51:01.259 --> 00:51:03.126
How about I profile you


00:51:03.127 --> 00:51:04.694
just for the fun of it?


00:51:04.695 --> 00:51:07.297
You ready?


00:51:07.298 --> 00:51:08.732
Not particularly.


00:51:08.733 --> 00:51:12.235
Yeah? Too bad.


00:51:12.236 --> 00:51:15.238
You left the amish community
when you were 18.


00:51:15.239 --> 00:51:17.340
Something happened,


00:51:17.341 --> 00:51:18.809
something your family
couldn't deal with,


00:51:18.810 --> 00:51:20.477
I mean, something you
couldn't deal with,


00:51:20.478 --> 00:51:23.246
so you bolted.


00:51:23.247 --> 00:51:24.814
Am I right so far?


00:51:27.551 --> 00:51:28.819
Right.


00:51:28.820 --> 00:51:31.855
So what's in that hole there?


00:51:31.856 --> 00:51:33.756
Or should I say who?


00:51:41.164 --> 00:51:43.166
Daniel Lapp.


00:51:43.167 --> 00:51:46.269
Who's that?


00:51:46.270 --> 00:51:50.207
A man who hurt me.


00:51:50.208 --> 00:51:51.708
And who put him there?


00:51:51.709 --> 00:51:53.276
My father.


00:51:53.277 --> 00:51:54.878
- Right. So he killed him.
- Why?


00:51:54.879 --> 00:51:57.280
No, he, um...


00:51:57.281 --> 00:51:58.815
He didn't kill him.


00:51:58.816 --> 00:52:00.382
Who did?


00:52:06.323 --> 00:52:08.758
I did.


00:52:08.759 --> 00:52:12.762
Oh, Kate.


00:52:12.763 --> 00:52:15.297
He raped me.


00:52:19.203 --> 00:52:20.537
Why'd you come here tonight?


00:52:20.538 --> 00:52:23.172
- To make sure
that he was dead.


00:52:24.208 --> 00:52:25.574
You didn't know?


00:52:30.213 --> 00:52:32.849
I thought he was our killer.


00:52:32.850 --> 00:52:34.216
Why?


00:52:45.795 --> 00:52:48.331
That's why.


00:52:48.332 --> 00:52:50.232
Oh, God.


00:52:56.339 --> 00:52:58.241
Tell me.


00:52:58.242 --> 00:53:00.310
- He, um...


00:53:00.311 --> 00:53:02.444
He worked on our
farm for years.


00:54:13.850 --> 00:54:16.286
I killed a man.


00:54:16.287 --> 00:54:17.754
In self-defense.


00:54:17.755 --> 00:54:20.557
- And now it's all
gonna come out.


00:54:20.558 --> 00:54:23.493
Do you know what that's
gonna do to my family?


00:54:23.494 --> 00:54:26.263
I'm not gonna tell anyone.


00:54:26.264 --> 00:54:29.332
I'm on your side, remember?


00:54:29.333 --> 00:54:32.034
I mean, somebody's got to be.


00:54:35.705 --> 00:54:37.539
Kate, you can trust me.


00:54:40.677 --> 00:54:43.579
You'll have to figure that
out on your own, I guess.


00:54:46.950 --> 00:54:50.654
That's nice.


00:54:50.655 --> 00:54:51.721
Thank you.


00:54:51.722 --> 00:54:54.824
You made it?


00:54:54.825 --> 00:54:57.494
Yeah, uh...


00:54:57.495 --> 00:54:59.428
When I miss my
family, I quilt.


00:55:02.732 --> 00:55:05.368
- You made the one in the
living room too, right?


00:55:05.369 --> 00:55:10.006
Yeah, and a few more upstairs.


00:55:10.007 --> 00:55:11.908
- Well, you must miss
your family a lot.


00:55:11.909 --> 00:55:13.610
Yeah.


00:55:13.611 --> 00:55:17.981
Well, I don't have a whole
lot left from my childhood.


00:55:17.982 --> 00:55:20.349
Actually, I don't have anything.


00:55:21.519 --> 00:55:24.486
After I left, that
was pretty much it.


00:55:28.491 --> 00:55:29.926
You know, when my Mom died,


00:55:29.927 --> 00:55:33.530
I didn't even get
to go see her.


00:55:33.531 --> 00:55:38.368
I got a call while
I was on stakeout:


00:55:38.369 --> 00:55:40.737
"She's gone."


00:55:40.738 --> 00:55:43.707
What'd you do?


00:55:43.708 --> 00:55:44.741
What to do?


00:55:44.742 --> 00:55:45.942
I...


00:55:45.943 --> 00:55:49.512
Sat crying half the night.


00:55:49.513 --> 00:55:52.816
And then I went
and made my bust.


00:55:52.817 --> 00:55:54.883
I'm a cop, so...


00:56:17.875 --> 00:56:21.544
Tomasetti.


00:56:21.545 --> 00:56:23.380
Yeah.


00:56:23.381 --> 00:56:24.913
Did you just kiss me?


00:56:25.983 --> 00:56:28.451
Damn. I-I think I did.


00:56:28.452 --> 00:56:30.720
- Just, uh...


00:56:30.721 --> 00:56:34.591
Just checking.


00:56:34.592 --> 00:56:37.160
How'd it go?


00:56:37.161 --> 00:56:39.863
Yeah, it was okay.


00:56:39.864 --> 00:56:44.134
Yeah, well, I'm, uh...


00:56:44.135 --> 00:56:45.134
I'm a little rusty.


00:56:46.470 --> 00:56:48.504
It's all right. Me too.


00:56:51.775 --> 00:56:53.743
I should go.


00:56:53.744 --> 00:56:57.447
Yeah.


00:56:57.448 --> 00:56:59.515
Are you sure?


00:57:03.753 --> 00:57:05.088
Good.


00:57:05.089 --> 00:57:08.591
You're not sure. All right.


00:57:08.592 --> 00:57:09.858
I-I'll see you tomorrow.


00:57:19.837 --> 00:57:23.106
- In painters mill, Ohio,
two bodies have been found,


00:57:23.107 --> 00:57:24.941
the first, a teen from
the amish community.


00:57:24.942 --> 00:57:27.043
We go now to sue
in painters mill.


00:57:27.044 --> 00:57:28.545
I have confirmation now,


00:57:28.546 --> 00:57:30.180
sources close to the
investigation confirm...


00:57:30.181 --> 00:57:31.681
Get me a list


00:57:31.682 --> 00:57:32.949
of all the moving
companies in the state,


00:57:32.950 --> 00:57:34.551
and give me the names
of their clients


00:57:34.552 --> 00:57:35.785
who left this area


00:57:35.786 --> 00:57:37.187
within six months of
the killings in '95.


00:57:37.188 --> 00:57:38.955
- Okay, and cross-check
it with a list of people


00:57:38.956 --> 00:57:40.623
who've moved back to
the area recently?


00:57:40.624 --> 00:57:42.459
Exactly.


00:57:42.460 --> 00:57:44.494
Hey, Kate.


00:57:44.495 --> 00:57:46.930
- Hey, Nate.
- What's up?


00:57:46.931 --> 00:57:49.833
- I'm really sorry I have
to give this to you.


00:57:49.834 --> 00:57:52.535
What is it?


00:57:52.536 --> 00:57:53.770
- I tried to speak
with the mayor,


00:57:53.771 --> 00:57:55.071
but he's just...


00:57:55.072 --> 00:57:58.641
Out of his mind with grief.


00:57:58.642 --> 00:58:00.642
I have to escort you out.


00:58:02.078 --> 00:58:03.879
What happened?


00:58:06.616 --> 00:58:08.218
I've, um...


00:58:08.219 --> 00:58:11.221
Been fired.


00:58:11.222 --> 00:58:13.756
- Well, then somebody's
not thinking right.


00:58:13.757 --> 00:58:15.959
- Uh, Mona, you and T.J..
- Have some work to do.


00:58:15.960 --> 00:58:19.629
I suggest you go and do it.


00:58:19.630 --> 00:58:20.964
- I can give you a
couple of minutes


00:58:20.965 --> 00:58:24.534
to gather your things
from your desk, but...


00:58:24.535 --> 00:58:25.702
- What do they think
I'm gonna do,


00:58:25.703 --> 00:58:27.570
vandalize the place?


00:58:27.571 --> 00:58:29.739
So who's going to run
the investigation?


00:58:29.740 --> 00:58:33.576
Well, for now, I will.


00:58:33.577 --> 00:58:36.846
- Well, let me know if there's
anything I can do to help.


00:58:36.847 --> 00:58:39.549
- I really appreciate
that, Kate.


00:58:39.550 --> 00:58:40.783
Hey, look, I'll speak
to the Council


00:58:40.784 --> 00:58:42.051
within a week or two.


00:58:42.052 --> 00:58:43.987
Of course, I can't
make any promises.


00:58:43.988 --> 00:58:49.859
But I'll try to get
you reinstated.


00:58:49.860 --> 00:58:51.728
And... and listen. I
hate to ask you this.


00:58:51.729 --> 00:58:54.697
But just bring the
car back tomorrow,


00:58:54.698 --> 00:58:55.731
if you don't mind.


00:58:58.134 --> 00:58:59.535
Right. Yeah.


00:59:32.135 --> 00:59:33.235
Kate.


00:59:39.142 --> 00:59:42.145
- Please tell me you
didn't do this to me.


00:59:42.146 --> 00:59:44.881
- Oh, Kate.
- No.


00:59:44.882 --> 00:59:47.283
- You told no one anything
that I told you last night?


00:59:47.284 --> 00:59:49.152
No.


00:59:49.153 --> 00:59:50.653
Come on. I swear.


00:59:50.654 --> 00:59:52.889
Auggie Brock has lost
it completely and...


00:59:52.890 --> 00:59:54.122
yeah.


01:00:00.663 --> 01:00:02.932
- Hey, I'm gonna stay
here until it's done.


01:00:02.933 --> 01:00:04.167
And when the...


01:00:04.168 --> 01:00:05.335
the dust settles,


01:00:05.336 --> 01:00:07.035
they're gonna come
to their senses.


01:00:08.038 --> 01:00:09.872
No, they won't.


01:00:09.873 --> 01:00:11.908
And you know it.


01:00:11.909 --> 01:00:13.343
- Well, at least I know
I'm not leaving here


01:00:13.344 --> 01:00:15.611
until... You're okay.


01:00:22.719 --> 01:00:23.885
Come here.


01:00:28.157 --> 01:00:29.291
Closer.


01:00:35.965 --> 01:00:37.299
Closer.


01:00:43.674 --> 01:00:46.208
You can come closer.


01:00:51.247 --> 01:00:54.250
What are you looking at?


01:00:54.251 --> 01:00:57.654
- I'm trying to picture
you as an amish girl.


01:00:57.655 --> 01:00:59.222
Oh.


01:00:59.223 --> 01:01:00.857
Is that so difficult?


01:01:00.858 --> 01:01:03.860
Well...


01:01:03.861 --> 01:01:04.961
You're a little, um...


01:01:04.962 --> 01:01:07.764
Assertive for an amish girl?


01:01:07.765 --> 01:01:10.266
Yeah, that's a good word.


01:01:10.267 --> 01:01:12.167
I was gonna say pushy.


01:01:15.738 --> 01:01:20.376
Well, I never said I
was perfect, so...


01:01:20.377 --> 01:01:22.077
You're a hell of a cop.


01:01:24.881 --> 01:01:28.785
Thank you.


01:01:28.786 --> 01:01:31.354
- That's about as good as I
get with the compliments.


01:01:31.355 --> 01:01:32.789
Understood.


01:01:32.790 --> 01:01:34.357
And...


01:01:34.358 --> 01:01:38.194
I'm probably gonna
screw this up.


01:01:38.195 --> 01:01:40.095
Me too.


01:02:16.432 --> 01:02:17.866
John.


01:02:19.936 --> 01:02:21.070
John.


01:02:21.071 --> 01:02:22.805
Mm.


01:02:22.806 --> 01:02:25.074
You awake?


01:02:25.075 --> 01:02:26.509
I've been thinking...


01:02:26.510 --> 01:02:28.044
Uh-oh.


01:02:28.045 --> 01:02:30.813
About our guy...


01:02:30.814 --> 01:02:31.814
Oh.


01:02:31.815 --> 01:02:33.249
And how he would have done it,


01:02:33.250 --> 01:02:36.119
how he would have gotten those
girls to come with him.


01:02:36.120 --> 01:02:38.121
Okay, I'm listening.


01:02:38.122 --> 01:02:40.323
- Well, he had to be
driving in broad daylight.


01:02:40.324 --> 01:02:41.524
- Right?
- Mm-hmm.


01:02:41.525 --> 01:02:45.061
- He sees a girl.
- He rolls down his window.


01:02:45.062 --> 01:02:46.863
And she's not scared.


01:02:46.864 --> 01:02:49.031
- Which you'd expect
after the first murder.


01:02:49.032 --> 01:02:50.833
- Exactly, the
mayor's daughter


01:02:50.834 --> 01:02:52.335
should have gone
running for the hills.


01:02:52.336 --> 01:02:53.870
But she didn't.


01:02:53.871 --> 01:02:55.838
- So it's got to be
someone they both knew.


01:02:55.839 --> 01:02:57.073
Or trusted.


01:02:57.074 --> 01:02:59.442
- Someone they both
felt safe with.


01:02:59.443 --> 01:03:01.811
- Yeah, or because
of their position,


01:03:01.812 --> 01:03:06.949
like a fireman or a
minister or a cop.


01:03:06.950 --> 01:03:08.251
I mean, let's not forget,


01:03:08.252 --> 01:03:09.819
he's got a real good
handle on forensics.


01:03:09.820 --> 01:03:10.987
One of my guys?


01:03:10.988 --> 01:03:13.556
- You know, just a
cop in the area,


01:03:13.557 --> 01:03:15.992
you know, or maybe a
doctor who grew up here


01:03:15.993 --> 01:03:17.859
and is comfortable with
the amish community.


01:03:22.365 --> 01:03:24.132
Are you expecting someone?


01:03:27.905 --> 01:03:29.372
Chief?


01:03:29.373 --> 01:03:31.406
Hey, chief, you there?


01:03:33.342 --> 01:03:35.211
- Hey.
- Sorry to bother you.


01:03:35.212 --> 01:03:37.246
I just wanted to, uh...


01:03:37.247 --> 01:03:40.950
- Can I come in?
- Yeah.


01:03:40.951 --> 01:03:44.287
- What's up?
- Uh, we made an arrest.


01:03:44.288 --> 01:03:45.521
What?


01:03:45.522 --> 01:03:47.023
Yeah.


01:03:47.024 --> 01:03:48.591
- Who?
- An amish man.


01:03:48.592 --> 01:03:50.226
Samuel hershberger.


01:03:50.227 --> 01:03:52.495
Samuel hershberger?


01:03:52.496 --> 01:03:54.063
That's not right.


01:03:54.064 --> 01:03:55.198
Oh.


01:03:55.199 --> 01:03:56.866
We got a pile of evidence.


01:03:56.867 --> 01:03:59.302
We got clothing from the
victims found in his barn


01:03:59.303 --> 01:04:03.105
and blood from the
victims on his floor.


01:04:03.106 --> 01:04:04.240
You don't buy it.


01:04:04.241 --> 01:04:05.308
No, I know Samuel.


01:04:05.309 --> 01:04:06.909
We grew up together.


01:04:06.910 --> 01:04:08.978
When we were kids, he used
to hand-tame wild birds.


01:04:08.979 --> 01:04:10.980
I saw him bottle-feed
a litter of kittens.


01:04:10.981 --> 01:04:12.381
I mean, he might be
a little simple,


01:04:12.382 --> 01:04:14.250
but there's not a cruel
bone in that man's body.


01:04:14.251 --> 01:04:16.385
I'm telling you.


01:04:16.386 --> 01:04:18.187
John, if there's evidence,
it's been planted.


01:04:18.188 --> 01:04:20.156
- Hold on.
- Jay?


01:04:20.157 --> 01:04:22.291
- Sorry, chief, I thought
you'd want to know.


01:04:22.292 --> 01:04:23.559
- Jay, wait.
- Do you want me to go?


01:04:23.560 --> 01:04:25.261
- No, you're fine.
- Yeah, who ordered this?


01:04:25.262 --> 01:04:26.529
Where is this coming from?


01:04:26.530 --> 01:04:29.565
Yeah, I understand, but...


01:04:29.566 --> 01:04:32.168
Yeah.


01:04:32.169 --> 01:04:33.970
I've just been
ordered back to bci.


01:04:33.971 --> 01:04:35.104
- When?
- Now.


01:04:35.105 --> 01:04:36.639
- They want me there at noon.
- Why?


01:04:36.640 --> 01:04:38.875
- It seems like the city
Council called them,


01:04:38.876 --> 01:04:40.443
ended my assignment,


01:04:40.444 --> 01:04:43.246
suspect in custody.


01:04:43.247 --> 01:04:45.448
You know, that's not procedure.
No.


01:04:45.449 --> 01:04:47.950
Someone is working
really hard here.


01:04:47.951 --> 01:04:49.619
T.J., who brought Samuel in?


01:04:49.620 --> 01:04:51.520
Who arrested him? Who
found the evidence?


01:04:51.521 --> 01:04:53.489
- Uh, Nichols.
- It was Nichols.


01:04:53.490 --> 01:04:55.057
Nichols?


01:04:55.058 --> 01:04:58.261
Nichols was an army ranger
for 15 years, right?


01:04:58.262 --> 01:05:00.162
- It can't be Nichols.
- He just moved here.


01:05:00.163 --> 01:05:02.131
Right. So he's a copycat.


01:05:02.132 --> 01:05:04.166
We just ruled that out.


01:05:04.167 --> 01:05:05.501
T.J., go to judge Rogers


01:05:05.502 --> 01:05:07.136
and see if you can slow
down the arraignment.


01:05:07.137 --> 01:05:08.670
- Got it.
- We'll be right behind you.


01:05:15.112 --> 01:05:17.413
- Mona?
- Chief.


01:05:17.414 --> 01:05:18.481
What's up?


01:05:18.482 --> 01:05:19.916
Thought you should know.


01:05:19.917 --> 01:05:21.483
Samuel hershberger
just hung himself.


01:05:24.054 --> 01:05:27.490
Yeah, she should be coming
up here in just a second.


01:05:27.491 --> 01:05:29.058
Oh, here she comes.
Here she comes.


01:05:29.059 --> 01:05:30.993
- Chief burkholder.
- Chief burkholder.


01:05:30.994 --> 01:05:32.428
- Chief burkholder.
- Here, please.


01:05:32.429 --> 01:05:34.496
What can you tell us
about this hershberger?


01:05:40.603 --> 01:05:42.672
Oh, my God, Kate. It
is just chaos in here.


01:05:42.673 --> 01:05:44.674
Okay, listen, don't
say a word to anyone,


01:05:44.675 --> 01:05:46.475
but I need you to check
Nichols' army records.


01:05:46.476 --> 01:05:47.677
Detective Nichols.


01:05:47.678 --> 01:05:50.012
Skid.


01:05:50.013 --> 01:05:52.415
- I'd swear I had him
take off his shoelaces.


01:05:52.416 --> 01:05:53.516
I mean, I'd have sworn.


01:05:53.517 --> 01:05:55.985
But...


01:05:55.986 --> 01:05:57.687
I fell asleep.


01:05:57.688 --> 01:05:59.522
- Do you know where
he was stationed?


01:05:59.523 --> 01:06:01.557
Uh, I think it was Georgia.


01:06:01.558 --> 01:06:03.526
- Yeah, Georgia.
- Okay, good. Start there.


01:06:03.527 --> 01:06:05.194
And double-check
where he grew up.


01:06:05.195 --> 01:06:08.497
- When... when did this happen?
- 1:00, 1:15.


01:06:08.498 --> 01:06:11.067
I couldn't have been out
more than ten minutes.


01:06:11.068 --> 01:06:12.201
Of course you can quote me.


01:06:12.202 --> 01:06:14.136
Just do me a favor, okay?


01:06:14.137 --> 01:06:16.339
I mean, he's a good cop,


01:06:16.340 --> 01:06:19.275
and I don't want to throw
the guy under the bus.


01:06:19.276 --> 01:06:22.378
And he's gonna retire
in two months.


01:06:22.379 --> 01:06:25.181
Yeah.


01:06:25.182 --> 01:06:27.483
Shoelaces. Can you
believe that?


01:06:27.484 --> 01:06:28.717
Who else was here?


01:06:30.387 --> 01:06:31.987
Nichols, uh...


01:06:33.557 --> 01:06:35.424
Nichols.


01:06:35.425 --> 01:06:36.726
- All right, I'm
here if you need me.


01:06:36.727 --> 01:06:39.395
Right, anytime.


01:06:39.396 --> 01:06:42.263
You too.


01:06:44.134 --> 01:06:45.768
Wow. Have you heard?


01:06:45.769 --> 01:06:48.637
Yeah, it's, um...


01:06:48.638 --> 01:06:50.172
Seems like all I
have to do is leave


01:06:50.173 --> 01:06:51.540
and the case gets solved.


01:06:51.541 --> 01:06:54.577
Well, we had more
than a little luck,


01:06:54.578 --> 01:06:56.479
both good and bad.


01:06:56.480 --> 01:06:57.747
I wish to hell you'd
have been here


01:06:57.748 --> 01:06:59.749
through the whole thing, Kate.


01:06:59.750 --> 01:07:03.652
What a mess.


01:07:03.653 --> 01:07:09.025
So what can I do for you?


01:07:09.026 --> 01:07:10.426
Samuel hershberger?


01:07:10.427 --> 01:07:13.362
Nate, I don't think he
could have done this.


01:07:13.363 --> 01:07:15.364
Why would you say that?


01:07:15.365 --> 01:07:16.565
Because I knew him.


01:07:16.566 --> 01:07:18.367
And he was so devout.
There's no way...


01:07:18.368 --> 01:07:19.635
Kate, how devout can a man be


01:07:19.636 --> 01:07:22.238
that rapes and bleeds
12 young women?


01:07:22.239 --> 01:07:23.606
But he didn't do
it, not any of it.


01:07:23.607 --> 01:07:24.774
That's my point.


01:07:24.775 --> 01:07:26.308
Well, why would
he hang himself?


01:07:26.309 --> 01:07:27.610
He didn't. Someone
else must have.


01:07:27.611 --> 01:07:29.145
Kate, Kate.


01:07:29.146 --> 01:07:31.447
Don't do this to yourself.


01:07:31.448 --> 01:07:32.648
Okay?


01:07:32.649 --> 01:07:34.483
You're a better cop than this.


01:07:34.484 --> 01:07:36.052
And you got some history here.


01:07:36.053 --> 01:07:37.420
Maybe that's why you missed it.


01:07:37.421 --> 01:07:38.621
- Nate.
- No, listen.


01:07:38.622 --> 01:07:40.289
Listen, it's...


01:07:40.290 --> 01:07:42.525
It's hard to accept when
it's one of your own.


01:07:42.526 --> 01:07:44.160
I understand that.


01:07:44.161 --> 01:07:46.729
I mean, I've got a soft
spot for your people too.


01:07:46.730 --> 01:07:48.130
Ever since I was a kid,


01:07:48.131 --> 01:07:49.331
every time I would
see one of them,


01:07:49.332 --> 01:07:50.733
I couldn't help but
think, "you know what?


01:07:50.734 --> 01:07:53.269
That just might be the
way to live life."


01:07:53.270 --> 01:07:54.537
They're good people, Kate.


01:07:54.538 --> 01:07:56.739
- That's right.
- You grew up in the area.


01:07:56.740 --> 01:08:01.277
- I sure did.
- I was born and raised here.


01:08:01.278 --> 01:08:03.279
- And then you went and spent
all that time in Alaska


01:08:03.280 --> 01:08:07.083
and, um... And shot a bear.


01:08:07.084 --> 01:08:09.652
- You need to think about
this a little bit, okay?


01:08:09.653 --> 01:08:12.755
Just clear your head.
Let it go.


01:08:12.756 --> 01:08:14.256
Go find yourself in Alaska


01:08:14.257 --> 01:08:15.724
and shoot a bear or two.


01:08:15.725 --> 01:08:17.726
- Yeah.


01:08:17.727 --> 01:08:19.695
You know what?


01:08:19.696 --> 01:08:22.565
I'm gonna write you one hell
of a recommendation letter.


01:08:22.566 --> 01:08:24.667
- I appreciate that.
- Yeah.


01:08:24.668 --> 01:08:26.836
No problem. Listen.


01:08:26.837 --> 01:08:29.638
I wish you the best
of luck, okay?


01:08:29.639 --> 01:08:31.674
Yeah, I wish you luck too.


01:08:31.675 --> 01:08:33.309
I got to go clear
my car out, so...


01:08:33.310 --> 01:08:34.710
Hey.


01:08:34.711 --> 01:08:35.810
No hurry.


01:08:43.586 --> 01:08:45.821
- Mona, forget Georgia.
- Bring up Alaska.


01:08:45.822 --> 01:08:47.223
What? Why?


01:08:47.224 --> 01:08:48.757
- Let me see every
murder by exsanguination


01:08:48.758 --> 01:08:50.259
in the last 20 years.


01:08:50.260 --> 01:08:51.660
- No, we checked that,
Kate, Nichols and me.


01:08:51.661 --> 01:08:53.162
There aren't any.


01:08:53.163 --> 01:08:54.630
- Just get me an officer
from the Alaska state pd


01:08:54.631 --> 01:08:56.165
on the phone.


01:08:56.166 --> 01:08:58.467
- Patch him through to my cell.
- Okay. Okay.


01:08:58.468 --> 01:08:59.835
Kate, Kate.


01:08:59.836 --> 01:09:01.470
There's something I
need to talk to...


01:09:01.471 --> 01:09:02.705
- Nichols, give me a sec.
- One sec.


01:09:02.706 --> 01:09:03.806
- Kate, I have Alaska.
- Thanks.


01:09:03.807 --> 01:09:05.774
Mona, I hear him fine.


01:09:05.775 --> 01:09:07.810
Lieutenant, this is
Kate burkholder,


01:09:07.811 --> 01:09:09.879
chief of police in
painters mill, Ohio.


01:09:09.880 --> 01:09:11.881
I'm working a homicide,
murder by exsanguination.


01:09:11.882 --> 01:09:13.849
We checked the lists on vcap,


01:09:13.850 --> 01:09:16.318
and there are no
entries for Alaska.


01:09:16.319 --> 01:09:18.721
- Murder by what's that?
- Exsanguination.


01:09:18.722 --> 01:09:20.356
And what is that?


01:09:20.357 --> 01:09:21.924
Bled to death.


01:09:21.925 --> 01:09:23.259
Oh.


01:09:23.260 --> 01:09:24.827
We don't use that term up here.


01:09:24.828 --> 01:09:26.629
What do you use?


01:09:26.630 --> 01:09:27.763
Bleeding out.


01:09:27.764 --> 01:09:29.165
- Well, then none
of our searches


01:09:29.166 --> 01:09:30.900
would have come
up with anything.


01:09:30.901 --> 01:09:32.434
Well, have you had any cases?


01:09:32.435 --> 01:09:34.336
Could be as far
back as the '90s.


01:09:34.337 --> 01:09:35.905
- Bled-out homicides?
- We've had a few.


01:09:35.906 --> 01:09:37.706
- Well, tell me,
have any of them had


01:09:37.707 --> 01:09:40.676
any sort of carved
figure on the abdomen?


01:09:40.677 --> 01:09:42.544
Oh, I can check.


01:09:44.548 --> 01:09:45.714
You know what?


01:09:45.715 --> 01:09:46.849
I think I remember
a case like that.


01:09:46.850 --> 01:09:49.285
Vic had kind of an
"x" cut into her.


01:09:49.286 --> 01:09:52.388
- A young woman?
- Yeah, far as I remember.


01:09:52.389 --> 01:09:53.489
- That's not an
"x." It's a 10.


01:09:53.490 --> 01:09:54.789
It's a Roman numeral.


01:09:59.261 --> 01:10:01.664
Chief?


01:10:01.665 --> 01:10:04.500
Burkholder?


01:10:04.501 --> 01:10:06.434
What happened to my line?


01:10:32.962 --> 01:10:34.897
- Yes, sir.
- I'm trying to get her back, sir.


01:10:34.898 --> 01:10:36.432
Mona, have you seen Kate?


01:10:36.433 --> 01:10:37.800
She was on a call, but...


01:10:37.801 --> 01:10:39.535
Yes, sir, I'll get
chief burkholder


01:10:39.536 --> 01:10:41.270
for you right away.


01:10:41.271 --> 01:10:42.504
Who is that?


01:10:42.505 --> 01:10:44.573
- It's a police
lieutenant from Alaska.


01:10:44.574 --> 01:10:46.575
- Alaska?
- No, sorry, sir.


01:10:46.576 --> 01:10:48.476
Her line is still busy.


01:10:49.812 --> 01:10:52.481
- You know what?
- I'll take that.


01:10:52.482 --> 01:10:54.683
Yeah, hi. This is
John tomasetti, bci.


01:10:54.684 --> 01:10:57.920
What's this in reference to?


01:10:57.921 --> 01:10:59.989
What year was that?


01:10:59.990 --> 01:11:01.991
Well, was the case ever...


01:11:01.992 --> 01:11:04.360
it wasn't closed?


01:11:04.361 --> 01:11:05.861
Yeah.


01:11:05.862 --> 01:11:07.930
Alaska.


01:11:07.931 --> 01:11:08.998
Where's detrick?


01:11:08.999 --> 01:11:09.931
I don't know.


01:12:04.453 --> 01:12:06.655
- Has anyone seen
detrick or Kate?


01:12:06.656 --> 01:12:07.823
What's going on?


01:12:07.824 --> 01:12:09.625
- I think you were set up.
- What?


01:12:09.626 --> 01:12:11.060
How do you know? By who?


01:12:11.061 --> 01:12:12.895
- Had to be detrick.
- Kate figured it out.


01:12:12.896 --> 01:12:14.563
Now I can't find
either one of them.


01:12:14.564 --> 01:12:16.799
She was just outside.


01:12:16.800 --> 01:12:17.900
Hey, hey, hey!


01:12:17.901 --> 01:12:19.101
Can we get a statement?


01:12:19.102 --> 01:12:20.769
- Gone.
- Okay.


01:12:20.770 --> 01:12:22.905
- Put out an apb on Kate's car.
- Okay.


01:12:22.906 --> 01:12:24.340
- And find me where
detrick lives.


01:12:24.341 --> 01:12:25.089
You got it.


01:12:35.884 --> 01:12:37.885
I know you're awake, Kate.


01:12:40.756 --> 01:12:44.559
No sense in keeping any
secrets between us now.


01:12:46.930 --> 01:12:48.764
Good job, by the way.


01:12:48.765 --> 01:12:51.399
I was beginning to wonder if
anybody would figure it out.


01:12:56.705 --> 01:12:59.941
Where are we?


01:13:01.945 --> 01:13:02.944
Home.


01:13:10.487 --> 01:13:11.753
Kate?


01:13:13.956 --> 01:13:15.923
Kate!


01:13:38.781 --> 01:13:41.015
Kate?


01:13:45.454 --> 01:13:47.055
So this is where you grew up?


01:13:47.056 --> 01:13:48.891
Yup.


01:13:48.892 --> 01:13:50.525
Cozy, isn't it?


01:14:00.068 --> 01:14:03.806
Something happen to you here?


01:14:03.807 --> 01:14:06.909
Plenty happened here.


01:14:06.910 --> 01:14:10.011
And I screamed and screamed,
but nobody ever came.


01:14:11.814 --> 01:14:15.551
You think that's
why I kill people?


01:14:15.552 --> 01:14:19.187
- I don't know why
you kill people.


01:14:20.190 --> 01:14:22.123
Well...


01:14:23.826 --> 01:14:25.060
It keeps the heart beating,


01:14:25.061 --> 01:14:26.727
I'll tell you that.


01:14:29.932 --> 01:14:31.833
It keeps the blood flowing.


01:14:35.103 --> 01:14:36.504
Mm.


01:14:40.943 --> 01:14:41.943
Damn it.


01:14:48.051 --> 01:14:49.551
Nichols?


01:14:49.552 --> 01:14:51.620
Yeah.


01:14:51.621 --> 01:14:53.555
Does detrick own
anything else?


01:14:53.556 --> 01:14:57.493
Apartment, farmland, anything.


01:14:57.494 --> 01:15:00.629
Wasn't T.J.. Working on a
list of abandoned properties?


01:15:00.630 --> 01:15:02.498
Yeah... Mona,
abandoned properties.


01:15:02.499 --> 01:15:03.699
I need that list now.


01:15:03.700 --> 01:15:07.069
- T.J.
- Right here.


01:15:07.070 --> 01:15:09.004
Still printing.


01:15:09.005 --> 01:15:10.839
- Uh, looks like
35 new ones here.


01:15:10.840 --> 01:15:12.007
Oh, man.


01:15:12.008 --> 01:15:13.709
What's wrong?


01:15:13.710 --> 01:15:15.110
- We got, like, 35
properties here.


01:15:15.111 --> 01:15:18.146
She's still printing.


01:15:18.147 --> 01:15:19.882
We're gonna have to
get as many people


01:15:19.883 --> 01:15:20.949
look for them as possible.


01:15:20.950 --> 01:15:23.752
And...


01:15:23.753 --> 01:15:25.186
Hold on.


01:15:27.089 --> 01:15:28.123
Where's skid?


01:15:28.124 --> 01:15:29.591
- Hey, skid.
- Yeah?


01:15:29.592 --> 01:15:31.193
Yeah, he's here.


01:15:31.194 --> 01:15:33.896
Didn't you tell me
detrick grew up here?


01:15:33.897 --> 01:15:35.297
- Yup.
- Where?


01:15:35.298 --> 01:15:37.165
Nothing... nothing
here owned by detrick.


01:15:37.166 --> 01:15:38.934
Yeah, he was raised
by his grandparents.


01:15:38.935 --> 01:15:41.603
- Mother's or father's side?
- Mother's.


01:15:41.604 --> 01:15:44.039
- Where... what's their name?
- They're dead now.


01:15:44.040 --> 01:15:47.175
That whole property's
been abandoned for years.


01:15:47.176 --> 01:15:48.277
Tomasetti.


01:15:48.278 --> 01:15:49.678
One more thing:


01:15:49.679 --> 01:15:50.979
Is there a town alarm?


01:15:50.980 --> 01:15:52.548
There's the firehall siren,


01:15:52.549 --> 01:15:53.948
just that and the church bells.


01:15:56.618 --> 01:15:59.688
- Call them all.
- Get everyone on it.


01:15:59.689 --> 01:16:01.256
- Amish too?
- Of course. Everybody.


01:16:01.257 --> 01:16:03.498
- 'Cause they have bells.
- Well, great. Get 'em ringing.


01:16:12.768 --> 01:16:15.070
Why the Roman numerals?


01:16:15.071 --> 01:16:16.137
Why not?


01:16:18.206 --> 01:16:21.175
- You left Ohio in '95.
- Why was that?


01:16:22.344 --> 01:16:25.147
I had a close call.


01:16:25.148 --> 01:16:26.848
Figured it was just
a matter of time


01:16:26.849 --> 01:16:28.649
before I got caught.


01:16:33.957 --> 01:16:36.123
So why Alaska?


01:16:37.293 --> 01:16:40.162
Wanted a little
more space to work.


01:16:40.163 --> 01:16:43.165
Right, your work.


01:16:43.166 --> 01:16:47.234
Girls six through ten, right?


01:16:55.277 --> 01:16:58.213
Why'd you come back?


01:16:58.214 --> 01:17:00.781
Look who's full of questions.


01:17:02.985 --> 01:17:05.621
Stalling for time?


01:17:05.622 --> 01:17:07.755
Huh?


01:17:14.897 --> 01:17:18.266
Who knows why I came back?


01:17:18.267 --> 01:17:21.069
You know, that's the
mistake you people make,


01:17:21.070 --> 01:17:25.240
trying to put some sort
of shape on all of this,


01:17:25.241 --> 01:17:28.977
trying to make
sense out of it,


01:17:28.978 --> 01:17:31.713
trying to find a meaning.


01:17:31.714 --> 01:17:34.316
You know...


01:17:34.317 --> 01:17:38.220
What about just some
girl in a green dress


01:17:38.221 --> 01:17:40.255
or a girl in a pair of jeans


01:17:40.256 --> 01:17:43.224
who walks across the street
and comes into view?


01:17:45.028 --> 01:17:47.396
It's random,


01:17:47.397 --> 01:17:48.363
100%.


01:17:48.364 --> 01:17:50.999
Sometimes...


01:17:51.000 --> 01:17:55.770
You just got to roll the dice.


01:17:58.274 --> 01:18:01.008
It doesn't have to make sense.


01:18:10.053 --> 01:18:11.752
Any last questions, chief?


01:18:12.922 --> 01:18:15.257
You don't have to do this, Nate.


01:18:15.258 --> 01:18:16.792
You're gonna get caught.


01:18:16.793 --> 01:18:18.693
You don't think they'd
figure this out by now?


01:18:20.263 --> 01:18:22.898
That's half the fun.


01:18:22.899 --> 01:18:25.132
Wait till they see
what I leave for 'em.


01:18:29.072 --> 01:18:30.905
What the hell is that?


01:18:32.075 --> 01:18:33.141
Kate!


01:18:33.142 --> 01:18:35.476
They're coming for you, Nate.


01:18:45.253 --> 01:18:47.054
Kate!


01:18:49.959 --> 01:18:51.059
Kate?


01:18:51.060 --> 01:18:53.929
Kate?


01:18:53.930 --> 01:18:55.497
- John!
- Kate.


01:18:55.498 --> 01:18:56.931
He's got a gun.


01:19:04.072 --> 01:19:05.307
Kate!


01:19:05.308 --> 01:19:07.309
He's going out the back.


01:19:07.310 --> 01:19:09.210
- Kate!
- Are you hit?


01:19:10.313 --> 01:19:13.148
I think maybe, yeah.


01:19:13.149 --> 01:19:15.182
Oh.


01:19:17.854 --> 01:19:20.020
- John, no.
- No, not now. Come here.


01:19:23.226 --> 01:19:24.326
- Come here, John.


01:19:24.327 --> 01:19:25.360
Come help me.


01:19:25.361 --> 01:19:26.762
Untie me. Okay.


01:19:26.763 --> 01:19:27.996
We're not gonna die in here.


01:19:27.997 --> 01:19:30.364
- No.
- No.


01:19:33.836 --> 01:19:35.871
- Get me the hell
out of here, John.


01:19:35.872 --> 01:19:38.339
- I was gonna say
the same thing.


01:20:21.050 --> 01:20:22.550
Somewhere around here.


01:20:25.220 --> 01:20:26.500
I'm gonna take a look down here.


01:20:48.443 --> 01:20:50.912
You're surrounded, Nate.


01:20:50.913 --> 01:20:52.580
It's no use.


01:21:06.394 --> 01:21:07.628
Well, what are you doing?


01:21:11.366 --> 01:21:12.433
Detrick, freeze.


01:21:15.070 --> 01:21:16.403
Shoot him, you're dead.


01:21:25.280 --> 01:21:28.048
It's finished now.


01:21:54.042 --> 01:21:55.943
Get out of here.


01:22:03.953 --> 01:22:04.985
Oh.


01:22:15.030 --> 01:22:16.998
- Hey, chief?
- Yeah?


01:22:16.999 --> 01:22:18.266
I just got a complaint


01:22:18.267 --> 01:22:22.203
about a loose cow at
stutz's farm again.


01:22:22.204 --> 01:22:24.204
Send T.J...?


01:22:25.240 --> 01:22:26.508
No.


01:22:26.509 --> 01:22:28.276
That's okay. I'll go.


01:22:28.277 --> 01:22:30.011
- Okay.
- Mona?


01:22:30.012 --> 01:22:32.414
Chief?


01:22:32.415 --> 01:22:34.248
I think we'll cite
him this time.


01:22:35.551 --> 01:22:37.351
Copy.


01:22:41.456 --> 01:22:44.259
So I'm heading back
to Columbus tonight.


01:22:44.260 --> 01:22:47.095
And I thought maybe
I could have


01:22:47.096 --> 01:22:50.130
dinner with the
chief before I go.


01:22:55.104 --> 01:22:57.205
All right.


01:22:57.206 --> 01:22:59.573
Okay.

